le at the same time, bringing exceptional and entertaining productions to Pittsburgh audiences,â said Paul Hennigan, Ed.D., president of Point Park. Alumni Michael Spagnoletti and Judge Guido DeAngelis Honored by Criminal Justice Club Monday, April 22, 2019 The Criminal Justice Club at Point Park University hosted a celebration dinner in honor of alumniÂ Michael Spagnoletti, â18, and Judge Guido DeAngelis, J.D., â80. School of Communication Graduates Part of Pulitzer Prize-Winning Team Wednesday, April 17, 2019 School of Communication graduates Ashley Murray, M.A., and Andrew Goldstein are part of the Pittsburgh Post-GazetteÂ team honored with a 2019 Pulitzer Prize for breaking news reporting. Alumni Profile Kidde Kokole '18 Meet Kidde Kokole, a 2018 Point Park University English graduate and Native Guest English Teacher for the English Program in Korea (EPIK). Alumni Profile Nick Davignon '18 After earning a master's degree in secondary education from Point Park University, Nick Davignon was hired by South Fayette High School as a long-term biology substitute teacher. Top 10 CNN Hero Honoree, City Housing Authority Official Speaking at 2019 Graduation Thursday, April 11, 2019 Point Park University will celebrate the annual Hooding and Degree Conferral and Commencement ceremonies Saturday, April 27 at PPG Paints Arena. Alumni Profile Ryan Bailey '14 \"I'm lucky enough to have been part of the first wave of esports talent. I'm one of the few who has a degree in broadcasting and real experience in a TV studio. I hope that more Point Park students can make their mark across the industry.\" Literary Arts and Social Justice Studies Department Presents Panel on Careers in Writing Thursday, April 4, 2019 The Department of Literary Arts and Social Justice at Point Park University hosted a career panel session March 28 featuring creative writing alumna Paige Mastrippolito â17, as well as writing professionals Maureen Passmore and Mariana Padias.Â History and Honors Programs Host Korean War Veterans Storytelling Session Monday, March 25, 2019 More than 150 Point Park University students, veterans, and members and guests of PittsburghâsÂ Veterans Breakfast Club attended a KoreanÂ War Veterans Storytelling Session March 20 on campus. Regional Premiere at Prime Stage Theatre Features Point Park University Alumni and Students Wednesday, February 27, 2019 \"Itâs comforting and exciting to see Point Park fostering connections with professional theaters. Itâs an example of the fact that training is working; script analysis, movement, and voice and speech are all pivotal to telling this story with justice,\" said Vanessa Vivas, theatre major. Alumni Profile Emily Marburger '10 '12 Meet Emily Marburger, mayor of Bellevue and a journalism and mass communication, history and MBA alumna of Point Park University. Alumni Profile Suzie Cool, M.A., '18 Meet Suzie Cool, M.A. in media communication alumna. Cool is manager of marketing and promotions, on-field host and color commentator for the Salem Red Sox. Alumni Profile Chelsey Driskel '17 '18 Meet Chelsey Driskel, B.A. in public relations and advertising and M.A. in intelligence and global security alumna, who was hired as a government contracts specialist by WESCO International, Inc. Alumni Profile Gabriel Florentino '18 2018 musical theatre alumnus Gabriel Florentino plays 'Manolin' in the world premiere stage adaptation of \"The Old Man and the Sea\" at the Pittsburgh Playhouse. Alumni Profile Miranda Peel '18 Meet Miranda Peel, a 2018 sports, arts and entertainment management alumna and guest experience services professional intern for Walt Disney World Parks and Resorts. Alumni Profile Annie Fiffick '16 Meet Annie Fiffick, 2016 Master of Science in criminal justice administration and food pantry director for Community Human Services. Student Profile Lauren Shoenberger '14 '19 Lauren Shoenberger, a 2014 business management alumna and M.S. in health care administration and management