ment Hosts Pittsburgh Police Recognition Ceremony on Campus Tuesday, December 18, 2018 More than 150 police officers and civilians were honored at the City of Pittsburgh Bureau of Police Inaugural Years of Service Recognition Ceremony Dec. 12 at Point Park University.Â Alumni Profile Brittany Bishop '17 Meet sports, arts and entertainment management alumna Brittany Bishop, marketing assistant for Live Nation Pittsburgh and live social contributor for the National Hockey League. Alumni Profile Hillary Maglin '15 As an editorial intern at Rachael Ray Every Day magazine, Hillary Maglin is gaining hands-on experience writing, covering events and posting to the magazine's social media channels. Alumni Profile Brianna Damich '17 Meet Brianna Damich, 2017 Master of Science in health care administration and management alumna and Midwest Region U500 Dental Sales Manager for Cigna. Alumni Profile Andrew Gall '07 Meet criminal justice alumnus Andrew Gall, chief of detectives for Beaver County District Attorneyâs Office. Alumni Profile Bryan Turner '18 Meet MBA alumnus Bryan Turner, corporate actions accounting supervisor and BNY Mellon's 2018 Asset Servicing Employee of the Year. Alumni Profile Jean Keene '12 Meet Jean Keene, a Master of Science in environmental studies graduate and environmental education specialist for Keystone State Park. Alumni Profile Jessica Joseph '17 \"Get an internship as soon as possible. You can sit in a classroom and learn all about how to use certain tools to help you create something meaningful, but nothing compares to experience. Internships give you an inside look into your desired field without working full time.\" Alumni Profile Samantha Crowe '14 Meet Samantha Crowe, a 2014 sports, arts and entertainment management alumna and marketing specialist for Comcast Technology Solutions in Colorado. Alumni Profile Sergio Flores '10 '18 Meet IT and MBA international alumnus Sergio Flores, a system integration technician for Bombardier Transportation. Alumni Profile Alexis Sherman '18 Meet Alexis Sherman, a legal studies and political science alumna who was hired as a paralegal for Kraemer, Manes & Associates. Alumni Profile Perris Drew '16 2016 theatre alumnus Perris Drew highlights his career as a professional actor and offers career advice to Point Park students. Alumni Profile Kenya Matthews '14 Meet Kenya Matthews, an information technology graduate of Point Park University and AVP for PNC, who was named to the New Pittsburgh Courier's Fab 40 Class of 2018. IT Alumnus, MBA Student One of 28 Veterans Across the Nation Selected for Google Summit Tuesday, November 13, 2018 Point Park University information technology alumnus and MBA student Jaime Ballesteros '18 was one of only 28 student veterans across the nation selected to attend the 2018 Google Student Veteran SummitÂ in Los Angeles. Alumni Profile Jessica Merritt '16 Meet Jessica Merritt, a Rowland School of Business alumna and customer success manager for Othot. Alumni Profile Faith Kraynik '17 \"My Point Park experience taught me how important collaboration and communication are to a creative production.\" Alumni Profile Kevin Dotson '16 Meet Kevin Dotson, human resource management alumnus and physician employment coordinator for UPMC. Alumni Profile Michele Tabaka '13 \"As a part of the advertising team at The Washington Post, I work closely with advertising agencies and marketing managers to analyze marketing needs and recommend appropriate advertising solutions per each clientâs budget,\" Tabaka said. Point Park University-Produced Film Premiers on WQED Thursday, October 11, 2018 Pennsylvaniaâs endangered watersheds are the focus of Downstream, a half-hour documentary produced by Point Park University's School of Communication environmental journalism program, in association with WQED Multimedia, and made possible through a grant from the Heinz Endowments. Alumni Profile Hana Rydl '15 '16 Meet Hana Rydl, a B.S. in biological sciences and an M.S. in environmental studies alumna, who was recently promoted to environmental inspector supervisor for TruHorizon Environmental Solutions. Alumni Profile Louis DeShantz '12 '16 Meet Louis DeShantz, an MBA and business management alumnus of Point Park University promoted to production planner for Uber's Advanced Technologies Group. Alumni Profile Tyler Jeski '15 School of Communication alumnus Tyler Jeski is the evening producer for WHP-TV CBS 21. Business Professor and MBA Graduate Are Among Authors of New Book About Pittsburghâs Engineering Triumphs Friday, September 28, 2018 Patrick Mulvihill, D.Ed., and 2017 on-siteÂ MBA alumnus Todd Wilson, P.E., are among the authors of the new book, EngineeringÂ Pittsburgh: A History of Roads, Rails, Canals, Bridges & More. Â Alumni Profile Nick Vizzoca '00 Meet Nick Vizzoca, a 2000 MBA graduate of Point Park University and president and CEO of Vincentian Collaborative System. 2018 Summer Journalism Workshop Friday, September 21, 2018 Alumni Profile Eric Holmes '18 Learn why Eric Holmes, City of Pittsburgh Bureau of Police commander and chief of staff, chose Point Park University and its criminal justice administration graduate program. Alumni Profile Thiago Siervo '18 Meet Thiago Siervo, M.D., from Sao Paulo, Brazil and learn why he selected Point Park University's MBA program. Conservatory  Named to Playbill.com Top 10 List for Broadway Representation Tuesday, September 11, 2018 âBeing perennially ranked among the most-represented schools on Broadway is confirmation of our Conservatoryâs consistent track record in developing successful artists,â said Paul Hennigan, Ed.D., president of Point Park. Alumni Profile Jason Kirby, DO, '17 Meet MBA graduate Jason Kirby, DO, center medical director for Clean Slate Addiction Treatment Centers and associate medical director for Highmark. Alumni Profile Michael Banks '14 MBA alumnus Michael Banks was recently promoted to senior staff accountant at Crown Castle in Canonsburg, Pa. TEDx 2018 at Point Park University Wednesday, August 22, 2018 Building Bridges â an independently organized TED event â brings together six innovators who will tell their own unique stories of bridge building. Join us from 9 a.m. to noon in the George Rowland White Performance Center, located in Lawrence Hall. Alumni Profile Heidi Ward '13 Film alumna Heidi Ward - a freelance producer in Los Angeles - won an Emmy for her work on an NBC television show. Alumni Profile Shannon Howard '05 '18 Assistant Principal Shannon Howard, Ed.D., earned a principal certificate from Point Park in 2005 and later returned to the University to earn a doctoral degree in leadership and administration in 2018. Alumni Profile Charles Youngs '16 '18 Meet Charles Youngs, a graduate of Point Park University's M.A. in curriculum and instruction and Ed.D. in leadership and administration programs. Alumni Profile Kelsey Diss '17 Meet Kelsey Diss, a 2017 post-baccalaureate accounting graduate and fraud analyst for Highmark. Alumni Profile Baylee Zimmerman '18 During her co-op with Flying Cork, sports, arts and entertainment management alumna Baylee Zimmerman was offered a full-time marketing coordinator position with the agency upon graduation. Alumni Profile Brittany Lauffer is Deputy Director of Communications for Pennsylvania Department of Human Services Since graduating from Point Park in 2016, Brittany Lauffer has worked as a multimedia journalist for Erie News Now, and is currently the deputy director of communications for the Pennsylvania Department of Human Services. Alumni Profile Emily DeShantz '12 '16 Meet 2012 cinema arts and 2016 MBA alumna Emily DeShantz, associate producer for Brunner in Pittsburgh. Alumni Profile Daria Opekunova '13 Meet 2013 international MBA graduate Daria Opekunova, customer operations manager for Misty Robotics in Boulder, Colo. Alumni Profile Justin LaBar '09 Since graduating from Point Park, LaBar has worked for Trib Total Media and World Wrestling Entertainment. Alumni Profile Anne Fullenkamp '10 Anne Fullenkamp, a 2010 MBA graduate, concentrated her degree in sports, arts and entertainment management and is now director of design for the Children's Museum of Pittsburgh. Alumni Profile Camille Guillot '07 '09 '14 Camille Guillot earned three degrees â a B.A. in public relations and advertising, an MBA and an M.A. in organizational leadership â from Point Park University and she is now a global partner marketing manager for Emarsys in Vienna, Austria. Alumni Profile Jenna (Petrini) Fraser '17 Meet Jenna (Petrini) Fraser '17, a graduate of Point Park University's Pennsylvania School Principal K-12 Certificate. Alumni Profile Rebecca Norton '18 Meet 2018 MBA graduate Rebecca Norton, a senior analyst for The Bank of New York Mellon. Alumni Profile 2017 Alumna Caite Miller Plans Events for Pittsburgh Magazine Meet Caite Miller, a 2017 public relations and advertising alumna, who is an events coordinator at Pittsburgh Magazine. Alumni Profile Caroline Loeser '15 Loeser's first professional dance jobs included the Pepsi Super Bowl LI Halftime Show and the Joanne World Tour with Lady Gaga. Alumni Profile Taren Lumley '18 Learn how Taren Lumley landed her internship with The Pittsburgh Foundation. Professor Kraniou Hosts Gathering of MBA Grads from his Macro-Projects and International Regimes Course Thursday, May 31, 2018 Point Park University MBA graduates who have taken the special topics course Macro-Projects and International Regimes, taught by Professor Dimitris Kraniou, Ph.D., over the past 30 years, gathered May 11 for a reunion celebration on campus.Â Creative Writing Alumni Launch Literary Magazine Spotlighting Science Fiction and Pop Culture Wednesday, May 30, 2018 Point Park University creative writing alumni Josh Hrala â12, Andie Fullmer '14 and Patrick Morris â14 founded The Arcanist, a web-based literary magazine focused on genre-based flash fiction and in-depth looks into pop cultureâs biggest stories. From Point Park University to Havas PR: Alumni Work for One of the World's Largest Communications Groups Thursday, May 24, 2018 Alumni Stacey Simon and Kariann Mano discuss their careers at Havas PR Pittsburgh and how their Point Park University experience prepared them for their roles. Alumni Profile Alumni Profile: Meet Stacey Simon, Account Supervisor, Havas PR Pittsburgh \"Having now experienced a range of industries and roles in the communications field, I can genuinely say that Iâm still thankful for my Point Park education to this day,\" she said. Alumni Profile Alumni Profile: Meet Kariann Mano, Assistant Account Executive, Havas PR Pittsburgh \"As an assistant account executive, I am responsible for creating content for social media, blog posts and newsletters, reviewing content for educational resources, media outreach to key trades and occasionally national media, and coordinate with vendors for trade show participation,\" she said. Alumni Profile Guillermo Velazquez '18 Meet 2018 MBA graduate Guillermo Velazquez, executive director of the Pittsburgh Hispanic Development Corporation. Alumni Profile Alethia Bush '11 Meet criminal justice administration alumna Alethia Bush, founder of The Center for Successful Reentry and case manager for the A. Philip Randolph Institute. Alumni Profile Adam Rivers '18 Meet Adam Rivers, a 2018 graduate of the M.S. in health care administration and management program. Alumni Profile Robyn Roux '12 Meet Robyn Roux, a 2012 global cultural studies graduate working as a Kindergarten ESL teacher in Hanoi, Vietnam. Alumni Profile Jose Flores '18 Meet Jose Flores, a 2018 information technology alumnus, M.B.A. student, veteran and Enterprise Architecture and Optimization Student Employee for U.S. Steel Corporation. Alumni Profile Erika Mangual '16 Meet Erika Mangual '16, a business management alumna and embedded control analyst for The Bank of New York Mellon. Global Cultural Studies and Dance Graduate Presents Research at American Association of Geographers Conference Wednesday, May 2, 2018 Lauren Gerlowski â who graduated magna cum laude from Point Park University this past Saturday with bachelorâs degrees in both global cultural studies and dance â recently presented a research paper at the American Association of Geographers 2018 Annual Meeting in New Orleans. Alumni Profile Matthew Veseleny '16 Meet alumnus Matthew Veseleny and learn how his M.B.A. degree from Point Park University helped him land his new position. Alumni Profile Jim Ice, Ed.D. Keynote speaker Jim Ice, Ed.D., is a trusted adviser to business leaders for more than 30 years. He was a member of the first class of graduates from Point Park's Ed.D. in leadership and administration program. Alumna and Assistant Superintendent of Allegheny County Police Maurita Bryant Honored by Criminal Justice Club Thursday, April 26, 2018 Alumna Maurita Bryant â06 â07 was honored with the Certificate of Excellence in Law Enforcement Leadership award April 17 by Point Park Universityâs Department of Criminal Justice and Intelligence Studies and Criminal Justice Club. Alumni Profile Nicholas Turgeon '16 Learn how 2016 graduate Nicholas Turgeon landed his position with the David L. Lawrence Convention Center in Downtown Pittsburgh. School of Communication Alumni Discuss Careers in Special Event Planning Tuesday, April 10, 2018 Three graduates from the Class of 2017 discussed their careers in special event planning - the good, the bad and the unexpected as part of the Distinguished Lectureship Series April 3 in the Center for Media Innovation. Networking in New York: SAEM Students Spend Spring Break Building Career Connections Monday, March 12, 2018 Sports, arts and entertainment management students and alumni spent spring break in New York City making career connections, meeting with industry leaders from Atlantic Records, Madison Square Garden, New York Mets and more. Alumni Profile Jocelyn Hyrb '17 Learn how an SAEM degree helped Jocelyn Hyrb '17, land her current position as a radio promotions manager. Alumni Profile Erica Messonnier \"Point Park shaped me into the performer I am today. The school provided me with all the tools I needed to become a professional performer. I am forever grateful for everyone who helped me achieve my dreams.\" Alumni Profile Fausto Severino '04 Meet Fausto Severino, Latin America Crosschecker for the Washington Nationals and SAEM 2004 graduate. Alumni Profile Alumni Profile: David Flora, Senior Producer/Editor, Detroit Pistons \"I believe I landed my current job because of my education and experiences in the field. I also made sure to have a clean and concise resume as well as a solid demo reel.\" Alumni Profile M.B.A. Alumna is Director of Communications for Central Catholic Learn how an M.B.A. degree from Point Park helped Chelsey Rovesti land her current position. Alumni Profile Shannon Shields, M.A. \"Changing careers was one of the best decisions Iâve ever made. Getting my masterâs degree from Point Park was the catalyst that allowed me to make that change,\" said Shannon Shields. Public Administration Program Celebrates its Alumni With Reunion on Campus Monday, December 18, 2017 From fire chiefs and EMS professionals to business and borough administrators, alumni from a variety of service professions were warmly welcomed at Point Park University's public administration reunion event. International M.B.A. Alumna Leading Information Technology Projects for PNC Wednesday, December 6, 2017 Meet Trupti Tamore, release testing manager for Kforce Consulting with PNC Financial Services. Alumni Profile Annie A. Pugh '17 Meet Annie A. Pugh, a fourth grade teacher at Lincoln Elementary, part of the Mt. Lebanon School District. Art Management Careers: Point Park Graduates Working for The Andy Warhol Museum Thursday, November 30, 2017 In their roles at The Andy Warhol Museum, alumnae Charlene Bidula and Lena Tavoletti are directly applying the knowledge and skills they gained in the sports, arts and entertainment management classes at Point Park University. Alumni Profile Charlene Bidula '03 '09 Bidula earned an MBA with a concentration in sports, arts and entertainment management in 2009 and a Bachelor of Arts in broadcasting in 2003, both from Point Park University. Meet Lena Tavoletti, Administrative and Financial Coordinator for The Andy Warhol Museum Thursday, November 30, 2017 Tavoletti earned a B.S. in sports, arts and entertainment management in 2013 and is currently pursuing her M.B.A. degree. Alumnus Marty Schiff Returns to Point Park to Teach the Next Generation of Filmmakers Wednesday, November 29, 2017 \"Being able to take my career and share it with the next generation of filmmakers is incredibly fulfilling,\" he said. Alumnus Marty Schiff Returns to Point Park to Teach the Next Generation of Filmmakers Wednesday, November 29, 2017 \"Being able to take my career and share it with the next generation of filmmakers is incredibly fulfilling,\" he said. Alumni Profile 2017 Alumnus is Managing Editor for The Northside Chronicle \"So many professors have aided me in my growth not just as a journalist, but as a writer, as a photographer, and as a videographer,\" said Neil Strebig. Alumni Profile M.B.A. Alumna Advances in Nonprofit Career to Director Position With Rivers of Steel Meet Carly V. McCoy, director of sales and marketing for the Rivers of Steel National Heritage Corporation. Alumni Profile Economics and Finance 2017 Grad Lands Position as Staff Auditor Soon After Graduating Meet Amanda Horn, staff auditor for PRGX USA, Inc. Fall 2017 Issue of The Point Now Online Monday, October 16, 2017 Get a peek inside the magazine for alumni and friends of Point Park. Public Administration Faculty, Alumna Provide Hurricane Disaster Relief Wednesday, October 11, 2017 Soon after record-breaking Hurricanes Harvey and Irma hit, public administration faculty Robert Skertich, Ph.D., Roy Cox, Ed.D., and Daniel Fitzhenry, Esq., as well as alumna Kate Jones Lambert, deployed to various regions in the south. Hospitality Focus: M.B.A., Business Management Alumnus Buys Restaurant in Bridgeville Monday, October 2, 2017 Meet Jason Simoni, president/owner of The Crafty Jackalope. Alumni Profile Managing and Marketing Music Artists: SAEM Grad Thriving in Arts Management Field Meet Carissa Atkinson, Founder/Artist Manager, Creative Direction Artist Management, and Marketing Director, River City Brass Band. M.A. Alumni Profile: Meet Angela M. Gaitaniella, Development Manager, Heinz History Center Tuesday, September 19, 2017 \"I am responsible for ensuring the successful execution of fundraising programs and events, donor cultivation and pursuing funding opportunities for all institution-wide initiatives,\" she said. Alumni Profile Alumni Profile: Angel Melendez '17, Service Engineer for IMS Systems, Inc. Melendez earned a B.S. in electrical engineering technology and was a member of Point Park's baseball team. Working for the NFL: SAEM Alumnus Captures Plays for the Philadelphia Eagles Friday, September 15, 2017 Meet David Wilson, Instant Replay Technician and Game Day Assistant for the Philadelphia Eagles. Theatre Production Alumnus Installs Stage Rigging in New Pittsburgh Playhouse Friday, September 15, 2017 \"Working on Point Park's new Pittsburgh Playhouse is amazing! I worked in the existing Playhouse in Oakland and am very familiar with those theaters. I can only imagine what faculty and students will be able to do in the new Playhouse,\" said Philip Irvin. Accounting and Dance Alumna Working for Ministry of Health in New Zealand Friday, September 8, 2017 Meet Kiri Richards, principal advisor, strategy projects, for the New Zealand Ministry of Health. Alumnae Ali Geroche and Anaya Bobst Land Prestigious Dance Internship with The Yard Thursday, August 24, 2017 Playbill Ranks Point Park as a Top 10 College on Broadway Tuesday, August 22, 2017 Political Science Alum, Analyst for Government Accountability Office to Speak at Convocation Monday, August 21, 2017 Meet Anthony Costulas, program analyst for the United States Government Accountability Office (GAO). Allegheny Conference Appoints Point Park M.B.A. Alumna as Investor Relations Manager Monday, August 14, 2017 Meet Patriece Thompson, investor relations manager for the Allegheny Conference on Community Development. Business Analytics Courses Connect M.B.A. Grad to Position With Duquesne Light Company Wednesday, August 9, 2017 Meet Jasmina Nikolic, business systems analyst for Duquesne Light Company. Producing Aristic Director at Lincoln Park Performing Arts Center is a Point Park Alumnus Wednesday, August 9, 2017 Behind the Scenes at WQED Multimedia with Point Park Alumni Alisyn Blackwell and Zak Boyle Friday, August 4, 2017 From Point Park to Pittsburgh CLO: Summer Season Casts Students, Alumni On-and-Off Stage Thursday, August 3, 2017 M.B.A. Alumna Leads Development, Branded Entertainment as VP for Spectrum Wednesday, July 26, 2017 Meet Samantha Morris, Vice President of Development, Branded Entertainment, for Spectrum. Point Park Alum Appointed Chair of Board of Trustees Wednesday, July 19, 2017 Working for the Stanley Cup Champions: SAEM Grad Discusses Role as New Media Coordinator Tuesday, July 18, 2017 Meet SAEM alumnus Evan Schall, new media coordinator for the Pittsburgh Penguins. Ed.D. Alumna Appointed Superintendent of Central Fulton School District Thursday, July 6, 2017 Meet 2016 doctoral alumna Michelle Hall, Ed.D. SAEM Alumna and Student Work in VIP at NKOTB, Paula Abdul, Boyz II Men Concert Thursday, July 6, 2017 Business Management Graduate Manages 43 Dunkin' Donuts Throughout Pittsburgh Area Wednesday, July 5, 2017 Meet Chelsea Halker '11, marketing and guest services manager for Heartland Restaurant Group. Musical Theatre Alumnus Connor Russell Stars as Flounder in Disney's The Little Mermaid Wednesday, July 5, 2017 Focused on Fashion in Pittsburgh: SAEM Alumna is the Founder of Style412 Discussion Series Thursday, June 22, 2017 Meet 2016 SAEM alumna Elysia Purnell-Newman. Alumni Profile Kelly Sasso \"The classes I took required that I go out and shoot and write stories on tight deadlines - sometimes solo, sometimes in a team - which is the exact skill you need when you take your first job,\" said Sasso. Point Park University MBA Alumnus Appointed New President of GAI Consultants Monday, June 19, 2017 Meet MBA alumnus Anthony Morrocco '10, president of GAI Consultants, Inc. SAEM 2016 Alumna Named Manager of Artistic Operations for the Pittsburgh Symphony Thursday, June 15, 2017 Meet 2016 alumna Kimberly Preloskly. M.B.A. Classes Benefit 2017 Graduate Working for U.S. Department of the Treasury Thursday, June 1, 2017 Meet Oliha Grichang, contact representative for the U.S. Department of the Treasury. Photojournalism Program Equips Alumnus with Skills to Excel in the Real World Thursday, June 1, 2017 \"I transferred to Point Park from Community College of Allegheny County because of the Downtown Pittsburgh location and the great communication programs. My father, who is also a Point Park alumnus, suggested the school to me. Photography was always something I was passionate about and when I was searching for schools, Point Park was one of the most well-rounded universities that offered a great photojournalism program.\" Engineering Students Design New Annunciator Call System for Turtle Creek Fire Department Wednesday, May 31, 2017 Residents in Turtle Creek Borough have experienced a greater sense of safety for the past two years, thanks to a thriving custom fire call annunciator system designed and built for the Turtle Creek Volunteer Fire Department by Point Park University electrical engineering technology students. Graduate Experience Prepares Alumna Jenny Snow to Present Thesis at National Conference Tuesday, May 23, 2017 Brandon Camic '16, '18 Wednesday, May 17, 2017 Meet Brandon Camic, staff accountant with Federated Investors, Inc., and a current MBA student at Point Park. Point Park Journalism Students Nominated for Golden Quill Awards Tuesday, May 9, 2017 M.B.A. 2014 Graduate Named VP, Senior Manager of Communications for PNC Monday, May 8, 2017 Meet Amanda Munsch, vice president, senior manager of communications, for PNC. Criminal Justice Club Honors Pittsburgh Police Chief Scott Schubert Tuesday, May 2, 2017 Culminating their focus on police appreciation this year, the Criminal Justice Club at Point Park University recently held a dinner honoring new Pittsburgh Police Chief and Point Park alumnus Scott Schubert. Bosnian Refugee, M.B.A. Alumnus Promoted to Supervisor of Pricing Operations at BNY Mellon Wednesday, April 26, 2017 Meet Elvir Muslimovic, supervisor of pricing operations for BNY Mellon. Pittsburgh Police Chief, Pulitzer Prize-Winning Photographer to Speak at 2017 Graduation Ceremonies Friday, April 21, 2017 Pittsburgh's New Police Chief is a Point Park Grad, Keynote Speaker at Hooding Ceremony Thursday, April 13, 2017 From Point Park to ABC News: Career Advice from Journalism Alumnus David Perozzi Monday, April 3, 2017 Perozzi - executive producer for ABC News in New York City and a native of Belle Vernon, Pa. - visited campus to discuss his professional journey and share career advice with School of Communication students. Alumna Gabriella Sorrentino is a Dance Captain for Hamilton | Broadway in Chicago Monday, March 20, 2017 Six Point Park Graduates Land Positions With Online Event Ticketing Company ShowClix Friday, March 10, 2017 Meet the Point Park University alumni working at ShowClix. SAEM Alumna Marketing True Runner, Chelsea Collective Brands for Dick's Sporting Goods Wednesday, March 8, 2017 Meet Rebecca Shore, marketing planning specialist and 2015 alumna. Regional Vice President of Operations for Comcast is a Point Park M.B.A. Graduate Tuesday, March 7, 2017 Alumnus Randall Tecza is a leader at Comcast. 2015 Alumna Caroline Collins is an Anchor and Reporter for WFMJ in Youngstown, Ohio Tuesday, February 28, 2017 \"Thanks to my knowledgeable professors and hands-on classes at Point Park University, I am living my dream! I am currently a television news anchor and reporter in my hometown viewing area, a station I grew up watching.\" South Sudan Native, Business Alum Recounts His Refugee Story at Center for Media Innovation Friday, February 24, 2017 Bior was invited to the CMI to discuss his harrowing experience as a refugee from South Sudan, the world's newest nation currently in the trenches of a civil war and devastating famine. Students Go Behind the Scenes at Cleveland Cavaliers Game with Alumnus Fred McLeod Friday, February 17, 2017 Alumna Advances in Adult Learning Field to President and CEO of Career Training Academy Tuesday, February 14, 2017 Meet Kimberly Rassau, Ed.D., president and CEO of the Career Training Academy. People of Point Park: Kyle and Alyssa Southerlin '11, First Impressions and Finding Love Thursday, February 9, 2017 Highlights from the Winter Issue of The Point Magazine Friday, February 3, 2017 Business Skills, Experience Gained in U.S. Help M.B.A. Grad Land Banking Position in Montenegro Friday, February 3, 2017 Dejan Duraskovic works for Addiko Bank in Montenegro. Cranberry Township Administrator Chooses Fully Online Public Administration Program Tuesday, January 31, 2017 Meet 2016 alumnus Jeff Gooch. BNY Mellon Analyst Discusses the Powerful Impact of His Point Park M.B.A. Degree Monday, January 30, 2017 Meet Stoycho Stoychev, Credit Management Report and Analysis Manager and 14-Q Corporate and CRE Loan Reporting Analyst for BNY Mellon. SAEM Alumna in Atlanta Promoted to Corporate Sales and Events Supervisor Tuesday, January 24, 2017 Meet April (Weber) Upplegger, Corporate Sales & Events Supervisor for Slingshot Entertainment. Recent Liberal Studies Graduate Working for Global Service Learning Organization Monday, January 23, 2017 Meet alumna Nina DelPrato, program assistant for Amizade. M.B.A. 2016 Graduate Profile: Diane Weston, Jewish Healthcare Foundation Fellow Friday, January 20, 2017 Meet Diane Weston, death and dying fellow for the Jewish Healthcare Foundation. Alumni Profile Sarah Meahl \"When I auditioned for Point Park's musical theatre program, I had a feeling that this was where I was supposed to be. My choice was so simple,\" said Meahl. CPA Firm BDO USA Hires Point Park Accounting Graduate as Tax Associate Monday, January 16, 2017 Meet Brett Gwosden, tax associate and 2014 accounting alumnus. Back to Top Point Park University 201 Wood Street Pittsburgh, PA 15222-1984 Careers at Point Park Location & Directions Non-discrimination Policy Privacy Policy Ready to learn more? Request information Plan a visit Take a virtual tour Calculate financial aid Follow Us tiktok instagram facebook Linkedin Â youtube Â Apply Now"
