    "https://www.pointpark.edu/careerready/Career-ReadinessCenter/index": {
      "title": "Professional Career-Readiness Center",
      "description": "Professional Career-Readiness Center | Point Park University | Pittsburgh, PA Skip to main content Menu Menu In this section In this section Apply Request Info About Us Academics Admissions & Financial Aid Career-ready Student Life Give Now Search Search Apply Request Info Events Calendar A-Z Quicklinks My Point Park Contact Us Career-Ready Career Center Career Opportunities & Support Handshake: Job and Internship Search Tool Information for Employers Meet the Staff Career Development News and Features Professional Career-Readiness Center Welcome to the Professional Career-Readiness Center The Professional Career-Readiness Center is an education and resource center that provides programs and services to enhance student success by creating opportunities to achieve career readiness, increase knowledge of career pathways, and connect to experiential learning such as internships and co-ops. The Center also assists students in developing professional skills and connecting to meaningful employment through strategic partnerships and targeted events. Individuals who utilize our programs and services learn to: Explore and understand career options, develop professional marketing materials, participate in the job search process, and successfully complete interviews Interact with business leaders, community members and employers through career-focused workshops, seminars and other networking opportunities Establish professional career readiness by developing and practicing competencies identified by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Participate in experiential learning programs such as internships and co-ops , in order to gain real-world, professional experience Key services The Center offers a wide range of services to help students and alumni tap into employment resources and opportunities: Jobs and internships Career fairs and workshops Jobs with the U.S. government Resources and handouts Meet the Staff Dean Jolin Director of Career-Readiness Read More Michael Clarke Program Manager, Experiential Learning Read More Kenneth Anderson Coordinator, Employment Recruitment and Student Engagement Read More Monica Ritter Career Counselor Read More Grace Thomas Career Readiness Assistant Read More Chris Rippee Neurodivergent Career Counselor Read More Testimonials \"As I near graduation from Point Park University with a degree in Economics and Finance, I reflect on the invaluable support I received from the Career-Readiness Center. My journey began with the guidance of Kenneth Lawson . Kenneth helped me polish my resume to a professional standard. The revised resume helped me secure an internship at PwC, which was vital for my next steps. In addition, Michael Clarke played a key role in helping me advance my internship credits and ensure that my work experience was recognized academically. I also had the opportunity to complete a Career Preparation course in my final year with Dean Jolin . His insightful feedback on assignments improved my academic skills and prepared me for real-world challenges. The combined efforts of the Career-Readiness Center staff played a pivotal role in my growth and success at Point Park University. I am extremely grateful for their dedication and support as I prepare to embark on my professional journey.\" – Jaume Genovard-Sanchez ‘24 \"I spent a lot of time working with the Professional Career-Readiness Center (PCRC) during my junior year. Career Counselor Monica Ritter helped me refine my resume, cover letter and interview skills. We spent time talking about the types of internships I was interested in, and she helped me lay out a timeline for applying. Shortly after, I secured my position at Cook MyoSite. I’ve been with the company since May 2022 and will start full-time employment after graduation. In addition to the help I received from the PCRC, I feel my experiences working with different offices and organizations around campus really helped my application stand out.\"  – Mara Van Thiel '23 \"In fall 2021, Michael Clarke and the rest of the staff in the Professional Career-Readiness Center encouraged me to participate in the Rowland School of Business Virtual Job Fair on Handshake to meet with several financial companies, such as First Commonwealth and First National Bank. S.R. Snodgrass was the last company I talked to at the event. Their human resources manager, Lenore Seifer, mentioned the firm had a not-for-profit division specific to offering external auditing services to nonprofit clients who need their financial operations examined. By the end of the day, I applied for the position. For my interview, I leaned on the tips I learned from the staff in the Professional Career-Readiness Center, and I was hired. I really enjoyed the work I did with Partner4Work Pittsburgh, so it was really exciting to land a job doing very similar work.\" – Steven Fisher ‘21 \"I picked Point Park University years ago because it had everything I desired - An intimate setting, invested professors, and access to career-defining internships. Point Park is the reason I have a career in Training and Development. (Keep in mind, I did not graduate in a flourishing economy.) As an alumnus, I'm so pleased to see that PPU is still actively supporting my career. It was incredibly easy to get back in touch with Career Services. The fact that I graduated more than a decade ago did not matter. Whether you're looking for a resume refresh, advice on continued networking, or an advocate in your job hunt - take advantage of being a PPU alumnus.\" - Rebekah Sedwick '12 Video: The Pathway to Professional Career-Readiness Schedule an appointment We'll work with you in one-on-one career counseling appointments at the Professional Career-Readiness Center — virtually or in-person — whichever works best with your schedule. Our office is open Monday-Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.  Saturday and evening appointments are also available. To schedule an appointment with a staff member, visit http://pointpark.joinhandshake.com/login . Contact us with any questions at 412-392-3950 or careerdev@pointpark.edu. Alumni outcomes According to the First Destination Survey of graduates from Fall 2023 - Summer 2024, administered by the Professional Career-Readiness Center via email from November 1 - January 31, 2025, 92% are employed or enrolled in a program of continued education. The Professional Career-Readiness Center provides our Alumni with a lifetime of services. We are available to work with graduates who are revising their career documents, want to practice interviewing skills, or are seeking assistance with the search and application process for their first post-graduation job or a new job opportunity.  We also work with Alumni who are returning to the workforce or are considering a new career path to reach their professional goals. We are also pleased to have local partners like the JFCS-Career Services , PA Career-Link - Pittsburgh , and Robert-Half who have provided wonderful support to our students and graduates as well. Pioneer Careers Podcast Bringing casual career topics into everyday life conversations.  Available on YouTube , Spotify , and Apple Podcasts . The 2023 - 2024 academic year produced 12 episodes and introduced listeners to 9 remarkable seniors (including co-host Natalea Hillen ) who recently completed degrees in acting, biological sciences, broadcasting, business, cinema/film, history, marketing, multimedia, sales, and sports communication.  Each of the guests shared insightful stories and addressed their goals, accomplishments, barriers, and the networking and resources they utilized in their own academic and career-readiness journeys that can shape or inspire the journeys of listeners. Point Park University 201 Wood Street Pittsburgh, PA 15222-1984 Careers at Point Park Location & Directions Non-discrimination Policy Privacy Policy Ready to learn more? Request information Plan a visit Take a virtual tour Calculate financial aid Follow Us tiktok instagram facebook Linkedin Â youtube Â Apply Now"
    },
    "https://www.pointpark.edu/NewsTagListing/Get-Career-Ready": {
      "title": "Get Career-Ready",
      "description": "Get Career-Ready | Point Park University | Pittsburgh, PA Skip to main content Menu Menu In this section In this section Apply Request Info About Us Academics Admissions & Financial Aid Career-ready Student Life Give Now Search Search Apply Request Info Events Calendar A-Z Quicklinks My Point Park Contact Us Get Career-Ready Get Career-Ready Â Check out more profiles in our Point Park POV series . Student Profile Austin Zarnick '26 \"If you want to be a filmmaker, Point Park's Department of Film and Animation offers amazing opportunities to reach your goals, especially in the B.F.A. film production program.\" Student Profile Ethan Villa '25 \"I would recommend Point Park to a prospective student because you have the option to live in the city where adventure is calling. There is so much you can do just walking around Pittsburgh, not to mention taking a bus to its many different neighborhoods.\" Student Profile Mady Thetard '25 \"I chose the B.F.A. theatre arts because I wanted to acquire a wide range of theatre skills and gain hands-on experience running a rehearsal room and putting up a script I wrote. I also loved how close Point Park is to so many regional theaters doing incredible work.\" Student Profile Michelangelo Pellis '26 \"Without Point Parkâs School of Communication, I would not be on the path to the career I always dreamed of.\" Student Profile Delaney Yeakle '26 \"Point Park has made me career-ready by providing me the opportunity to learn from talented professors with years of experience in my chosen career field. They bring so much knowledge to class from their real-world experiences and prepare us to enter the workforce confidently.\" 2024 Highlights Friday, December 27, 2024 From our acceptance into the NCAA to the inauguration of our ninth president, it was an eventful year for the Pioneers. Student Profile Bianca Dixon '28 \"Point Park's Pittsburgh Playhouse is beautiful. The dance studios, the workspaces, the performance spaces, there's so much to talk about. I love spending time there and it really is a privilegeÂ as a student at Point Park.\" Student Profile Anne Barbosa '26 \"Point Park has shown me the diversity of opportunities available with my major, and the downtown location puts me right in the heart of the city, making it easy to network and explore job prospects.\" Student Profile Daniel Salas '25 \"What I love most about living in Pittsburgh is the variety of entertainment the city offers. Thereâs always something to do, and I never get bored. I also love learning here because the opportunities are endless, no matter what youâre studying.\" Student Profile Kairi Stallsmith '24 \"Point Park has made me career-ready by encouraging me to try new activities and learn from my mistakes. As a student teacher, I have success with lesson plans, but I also experience failures. In both instances, I improve my skills as a teacher.\" Student Profile Devyn Amigh '26 \"It all came together that I made the right decision to major in broadcasting when I sat behind the U-View desk my freshman year. Feeling the studio lights on my face and testing my mic before starting the show hit me, and I knew I was in the right place.\" Student Profile Ashley Boynes-Shuck '24 \"The M.A. in Professional Studies allowed me to transfer my previous credits in, and I was able to tailor my course selections to fit in with not only my professional experience up until this point, but also next steps in my career moving forward.\" Student Profile Jared Topping '24 \"Point Park's marketing and sales program helped me find my passion for selling while taking a wide variety of courses across many different majors.\" Student Profile AJ de la Cruz '25 \"Point Park offers a range of coursework to suit the needs and passions of students. The professors find joy in what they do. Faculty and staff who have chosen to dedicate themselves to students' betterment are readily available for support.\" Student Profile Joel Balinao '27 \"Point Parkâs B.F.A. musical theatre program is one of the best in the country. Not only does it have access to amazing facilities, but it also has a really welcoming, heartwarming and open-minded group of faculty and staff.\" Student Profile Evan Carter '26 \"What I enjoy about the engineering program are the professors and the effort that they put into helping us achieve success. They are kind, incredibly helpful and committed to inspiring us to become better people in and out of the classroom.\" Student Profile Harmony Sheftall '26 \"Point Park's PR, advertising and social media program met all of my criteria and more. It was important to me to find a university that had designated resources for my major, got me out of my hometown and had the integrity as an institution to open doors to connections and opportunities.\" Student Profile Teagan deGroen '24 \"I chose Point Park for many reasons, but primarily because of the experiences and opportunities available. From my first semester, I was working on shows with upperclassmen, professors and national and local industry professionals.\" Student Profile Devon McGee '25 \"Point Park provides its students with valuable professional experiences. In the psychology and sports, arts, entertainment & music business programs, I have been exposed to opportunity after opportunity to make professional connections early in my college career.\" Student Profile Gwendolyn Hessom '25 \"At Point Park, students discover and engage in their passions. The instructors, degree programs and student organizations provide everyone with the ability to find what they love and immerse themselves in it.\" Student Profile Natalie Caine '25 \"The interdisciplinary studies major at Point Park has allowed me to pursue a multitude of fields that interest me. I am able to gain critical insight and experience through a creative lens. Point Park has given me a truly unique educational opportunity.\" 2023 Year in Review Wednesday, December 27, 2023 From electing a new president to charting a bold path forward to shape the University's future, Point Park is celebrating our highlights from 2023. Take a look back at some of our top stories of the year. Student Profile Estella Persio '24 \"One of the reasons I chose Point Park is because of the George Rowland White Performance Center. It's a dream to train in the beautiful dance studios during my college career.\" Student Profile Brandon Cunningham '23 \"Point Park is like no other university. There is a city vibe on the college campus. Being in a centralized location where there is live entertainment allows students to fully immerse themselves in the vibrant attractions in Pittsburgh.\" Student Profile Adam Snook '24 \"I chose the B.A. cinema arts program because cinema students are on set their ï¬rst semester. This hands-on experience helps you discover so much about your future career path.\" Student Profile Indya Durham '24 \"The sports communication program is very hands-on and I love that. I feel prepared to take on any assignment and ready for the real world.\" Student Profile Juan Barrera '25 \"Point Park's downtown location provides ample internship and co-op opportunities with local businesses, facilitating practical experience and professional networking.\" Student Profile Haze Basped '26 \"Point Park is more than just an educational institution; it's a community. Its small size ensures everyone knows you, and the diverse student body ensures you'll find your people, making lifelong friendships along the way.\" Student Profile Madison Downing '24 \"From the moment I learned about the many different jobs in theatre, I immediately knew I couldnât just do one thing. The theatre arts program encourages exactly that. This program has molded me into a well-rounded performer, director, playwright, producer and so much more.\" Student Profile Nila Payne '26 \"Point Park is really a special place, and youâll get opportunities here that you wonât get anywhere else. In less than two years, Point Park has helped me grow into a better and more confident person, especially from a career perspective.\" Student Profile Tessa Williams '25 As part of her practicum, digital journalism major Tessa Williams photographed the work of the mission team in Antigua, Guatemala, during Operation Walk Pittsburgh's Mission 2023 trip. Student Profile David Keyser '23 \"Point Park is an overall amazing school, from the classes and faculty to the beautiful city campus. It feels like a family here, and I couldnât imagine my life anywhere else.\" Student Profile Hudson Hartley '23 \"Jenna Lo Castro and Camille DowningÂ are my favorite professors. They help students with internship opportunities, resume building and how to create an online portfolio. They have impacted not just my education, but my outlook on life.\" Student Profile Caitlyn Scott '23 \"The flexible structure of the journalism program allows students to gain experience in print writing, broadcasting and multimedia composition. Itâs important to have a variety of options to choose from and the freedom to focus on specific areas of interest.\" Student Profile Kaitlyn Caiarelli '24 \"Point Park University's School of Education is preparing me for a career in education by offering courses that include real-world experience out in the field.\" Student Profile Nadia Jones '25 \"If you truly are passionate and driven to achieve a specific goal or dream, the faculty and staff at Point Park will do everything in their power to get you to that goal. This is a major characteristic to consider when looking for a school because it takes a village to build a successful career, and you want to build it with people who care. Point Park cares.\" Student Profile Olivia Lehman '25 \"Point Park provides connections and resources for students to build a successful life after college. Students are able to establish meaningful relationships with faculty, which can lead to a greater chance of opportunity within their desired field. The faculty at Point Park care about their students and want them to succeed, motivating them to put their best work and their best foot forward.\" Student Profile Miguel Salvador '23 \"There is a great sense of community at Point Park. It is a fairly small university, but the advantage of that is you are not just a number here on campus. You can make valuable connections with the faculty and staff throughout your time at Point Park.Â The resources here, such as the professors, networking opportunities and the ability to gain hands-on experience, will help you become successful in your career.\" Student Profile Tia Ellison '23 \"I chose the public relations, advertising and social media program because I knew that it would provide me well-rounded communication skills and the chance to engage in real-world opportunities.\" Student Profile Natalia Zucco '23 \"Thereâs a great opportunity to learn at Point Park, and not just in the classroom. Beyond learning about your major, you learn about people, relationships, society and yourself. There are so many students representative of different communities, cultures and countries. Point Park's environment fosters opportunities for students to develop new ideas and realize how much there is to explore and experience in this world.\" Student Profile Shivansh Waleacha '23 \"Point Park is one of the most welcoming environments I've ever experienced. You can be from anywhere, from any background, and feel like you are a part of something bigger than yourself at this school.\" Student Profile Allison Mullin '23 \"The connections and resources that Point Park offers are helping me prepare for my career. The faculty, especially the criminal justice professors, have real-life experience and often share those experiences with students. I've utilized theÂ Professional Career-Readiness Center since junior year, which has helped me connect with potential employers and find internships.\" Student Profile Cole Sholtis '24 \"Point Park serves as a perfect school for expanding upon my creative and technical skills to tell a story in the cinema arts program, and also challenges me academically in the accounting program.\" Student Profile Andrew Bensch '23 \"Point Park is preparing me for career success because the classes I am taking are relevant to what I want to pursue. I am excited for next semester because I will be taking two classes about archiving. I often find that what I learn in class, I can immediately apply to my archival work for West View Borough, and vice versa.\" Student Profile Ava Cook '24 \"When you attend Point Park, your professors make an effort to know your name, get to know you on a personal level and you will take courses with many of the same classmates throughout your educational career, allowing you to form close bonds with people in your major.\" Student Profile Nate Kelly '23 \"Having transferred, I can say from experience few colleges have programs that ensure students are prepared for their field quite like Point Park. Professors go the extra mile to connect students with companies and try to set every student up for a successful career after college.\" Student Profile Sophie Jebose '23 \"What I love the most about Point Park's elementary education program is the Matt's Maker Space Lab. I have most of my classes in the maker space, and the setup is great for hands-on learning.\" Student Profile Jenna Clover '24 \"I encourage anyone who is interested in majoring in musical theatre to seriously consider Point Park â I have grown in ways I never thought possible.\" Student Profile Jake Dabkowski '23 \"Thereâs so much culture in Pittsburgh, and being able to experience it unfiltered is one of the coolest things about going to Point Park. It is far more fulfilling than going to a school that is just a campus and nothing else.\" Student Profile Sandamini Sinley '25 \"I chose Point Park because the campus is embedded in Pittsburgh's business district, the faculty create opportunities for students to collaborate with working professionals to gain more real-world experience in class and the University offered me a generous financial aid package.\" Student Profile Hannah Lanham '24 \"I was drawn to Point Park for the internship opportunities offered, as well as the high percentage of students who get a job directly after graduation.\" Back to Top Point Park University 201 Wood Street Pittsburgh, PA 15222-1984 Careers at Point Park Location & Directions Non-discrimination Policy Privacy Policy Ready to learn more? Request information Plan a visit Take a virtual tour Calculate financial aid Follow Us tiktok instagram facebook Linkedin Â youtube Â Apply Now"
    },
    "https://www.pointpark.edu/NewsTagListing/Alumni News": {
      "title": "Alumni News",
      "description": "Alumni News | Point Park University | Pittsburgh, PA Skip to main content Menu Menu In this section In this section Apply Request Info About Us Academics Admissions & Financial Aid Career-ready Student Life Give Now Search Search Apply Request Info Events Calendar A-Z Quicklinks My Point Park Contact Us Alumni News Alumni News Alumni Profile Delaney Pater '25 \"What stood out to me about Point Park University was that students were animating on day one of the program, whereas most other animation programs push animation classes back to sophomore year.\" Emily Zutz '26 Tuesday, September 1, 2026 \"I was consistently impressed with the content provided in my classes and how much it was based on current research and instructional practices. Even though I have spent over a decade in the classroom, I still learned about practices that I could put into place the next day.\" Alumni Profile Ian Lewis '17 \"Iâve been lucky to have been a part of many Marvel Cinematic Universe films and TV shows. Iâve stood on the same sets with all three live-action Spider-Men and scaled rooftops with Daredevil.\" Point Park University Alumni Went From Stage AE Internships to General Managers in Pittsburgh, Columbus Thursday, June 18, 2026 After taking their first steps through internships, two Point Park University alumni are managing major venues in their cities. Alumni Profile Rev. LaWana Butler '19 Lending a helping hand to those looking to change their life, the work that LaWana Butler, Ph.D., does each day is made possible through her experiences at Point Park University. Alumni Profile Alison Maternowski '12 Working as a general manager for KEMBA Live and a director of operations at PromoWest/AEG, Alison Maternowski uses the skills learned through real-world experiences earned at Point Park to keep things running smoothly. Alumni Profile Payton Comunale '21 Payton Comunale '21 is a marketing campaign coordinator for the Pittsburgh Steelers. Point Park University Celebrates 66th Commencement and Hooding Ceremonies Tuesday, May 12, 2026 Point Park University celebrated graduation at Petersen Events Center on Friday, May 8. Pittsburgh Mayor Corey O'Connor was the commencement speaker. Alumni Profile Hope Debelius '22 Hope Debelius highlights how the theatre production: design program prepared her for a career as a lighting designer. Alumni Profile Delaney Metikosh '24 While no two days are the same in sports, Delaney is using her degree to expertly support the Pittsburgh Penguins Foundation. Alumni Profile Ashley Rose Zimmerman '14 Point Park dance degree prepares alumna Ashley Rose Zimmerman to take flight as an aerialist for Ringling Bros. and Barnum & Bailey. Michael P. Pitterich Sales and Innovation Summit 2026 Tuesday, March 24, 2026 Students, alumni, and business leaders gathered to learn about the ever-changing sales industry and honor those making an impact in Pittsburgh's business scene. Alumni Profile Jeremy Olson '11 \"What I learned is that career paths are rarely a straight line; you might have to take a job that feels off the beaten path, but just keep your goals in mind, get your foot in the door, make connections and learn from others.\" Alumni Profile Erica Rodriguez '19 \"For students who are analytical, curious and motivated by service, intelligence studies provides a challenging yet rewarding path with diverse career opportunities across multiple agencies and disciplines.\" Alumni Profile Elena LaQuatra '14 \"With campus being in the heart of Downtown Pittsburgh, I was able to spend time shadowing several local journalists and with the help of my professors, I secured internships with two of the news stations while completing my classes.\" Alumni Profile Holly Hagle '06 Holly Hagle is both an alumna and an adjunct in the School of Education. She was recently appointed president of the Association for Medical Education and Research in Substance Abuse. Alumni and Students' Work Featured at Artists Image Resource Wednesday, March 11, 2026 The work of 13 Point Park University students and alumni will be showcased in \"Hallucinations\" at Artists Image Resource and is free and open to the public. Alumni and Current Students Share Advice, Personal Journeys at Literature, Culture and Society Career Summit Monday, March 2, 2026 Point Park University students and alumni formed a panel to share their experiences with finding jobs and internships during the recent Literature, Culture and Society Job and Internship Summit on Feb. 25, 2026. Bob Pompeani High School Broadcast Award Wednesday, February 25, 2026 The Pompeani Award recognizes the best high school broadcast show in Pennsylvania, OhioÂ and West Virginia. Alumni Profile Claire Medinis '22 Claire Medinis '22 highlights how her undergraduate dance training and experience prepared her for a career as a stuntwoman for film /TV. Anna Cannavo '23 Combines Dance and Education Degrees in Role as Dance Team Coach Thursday, February 5, 2026 \"Point Park provides a unique experience for students with its vast program options and ability to help you find your niche. For me, that meant pursuing dance and education, and now the school offers aÂ fast-track B.F.A. to M.Ed. programÂ for dancers and educators to do just that.\" Alumni Profile Sam Kronhaus '23 \"Point Park's theatre production: stage-management program prepared me for a career in professional theatre through intensive, hands-on training that mimicked the professional world,\" said Sam Kronhaus '23. \"The Chief\" Stars Professor and Alumnus Monday, January 26, 2026 \"The Chief\" is a one-man play that brings the spirit of Pittsburgh football and the legacy of Art Rooney to the stage Feb. 4â8, 2026, in the Highmark Theatre. Alumni Profile Gavin Anderson '24 \"I really liked how dynamic Point Park's broadcasting program was. I acquired so many different skills, including editing, writing, interviewing techniques and videography.\" Alumni Perform in Rockettesâ 100th Anniversary Season Wednesday, December 17, 2025 Seven Point Park alumni are performing this holiday season in the Rockettes Holiday Show at Radio City Music Hall, as the Radio City Rockettes celebrate their 100th anniversary. Alumni Profile Olivia Busby '20 \"I chose Point Park because it had everything I wanted. It was in a bigger city than my hometown and I also loved that I would start making films immediately in my freshman year.\" Alumni Profile Dana Drewniak '17 While no two days look the same in live sports, Dana Drewniak uses experience gained from her SAEM degree to ensure that Cleveland Cavalier's games are exciting events. Sidra Bell Dance New York Headlines 2025 Fall Into Dance Festival Wednesday, December 10, 2025 Sixty high school students attended Point Park University's Fall Into Dance Festival, a two-day program featuring master classes and conversations with industry professionals, as well as a college fair to explore opportunities in the performing arts.Â Alumni Profile Annalee (Tomak) Cross '16 '26 \"If you are looking for small class sizes, hands-on experience and access to industry professionals, Point Park University is the perfect place for you. If I had gone to a larger school, I would not be where I am in my career.\" Alumni Profile Caroline Inches '24 \"As a theatre production: stage-management major, students get to be an assistant stage-manager during their first semester on a main stage show, which is not common at other universities across the country.\" Aspiring Filmmakers Showcase Their Work at Steel City High School Film Festival Friday, October 17, 2025 Aspiring filmmakers showcased their work and gained hands-on experience at Point Park University's Inaugural Steel City High School Film Festival. SAEM Business Students Volunteer at 2025 IEBA Conference Thursday, October 16, 2025 Students from Point Park University's Sports, Arts, Entertainment and Music Business program traveled to Nashville to volunteer and tour historic venues. Alumni Profile Chloe Troutman '23 Chloe Troutman was selected as this fall's Matt's Maker Space Fellow in Ireland, where she teaches at an international school. Alumni Profile Meghan Manning '14 \"I was so happy to visit Point Park to share my industry experiences with senior jazz students. I spoke about my career path since graduating from Point Park, how I've been able to pivot to sustain a long dance career and answered their questions.\" Point Park Makes Playbill List of Most Alumni Performing in 2024-25 Broadway Season Thursday, September 11, 2025 âWe are honored to be included on this prestigious list. Itâs wonderful to see Point Park University alumni working on the most famous stages in the world,â said Gary Kline, associate dean and artistic director, School of Theatre, Film and Animation. 2025 Musical Theatre Summer Intensive Highlights Wednesday, July 30, 2025 High school students explored acting, dancing and singing at Point Park University's inaugural Musical Theatre Summer Intensive. End-of-Year and Senior Week Celebrations Wrap Up 2024-25 Academic Year Wednesday, May 14, 2025 Schools within the University celebrated the academic accomplishments of students, while the offices of Student Life and Alumni hosted special gatherings for graduates, and the Outstanding Student Awards recognized accomplishments of students of all years, in academic, athletic, leadership and other categories. Point Park University Celebrates 65th Commencement and Hooding Ceremonies Monday, April 28, 2025 Point Park University celebrated graduation at PPG Paints Arena on Saturday, April 26. Rowland School of Business Clubs Collaborate with Professional Career-Readiness Center, Alumni on Networking Event Monday, April 28, 2025 The Student Accounting Association, Student Human Resources Association and Pioneer Tech Innovators brought students, faculty and alumni together to practice their networking skills in real time and gain valuable insights from the Professional Career-Readiness Center's staff. Giulia Follador '24 '25 Friday, April 25, 2025 Giulia Follador, a volleyball player from Turin, Italy, is driven to connect international students and build community. Sports Sales Force Thrives at Point Park University, Inspires New Sports Management Program Tuesday, April 22, 2025 Point Park University students in the Sports, Arts, Entertainment & Music Business program and the new Sports Management program have access to a wealth of experiential learning opportunities to prepare them for sports sales roles. Alumni Profile Maria Brucker Collins '19 \"I loved how well-rounded Point Park's civil engineering program was. The many different lab courses we did gave us hands-on experience with how different subjects and theories actually work.\" Alumni Profile Aaron Cooney '12 Alumnus Aaron Cooney, broadcaster and digital content producer for the San Diego Gulls, made his NHL broadcasting debut calling the Anaheim Ducks' game versus the Pittsburgh Penguins. Chemistry Carnival Provides Education Majors with Real-World STEM Teaching Experience Tuesday, March 18, 2025 The R&D Impact Foundation recently partnered with Point Park University's School of Education to design and facilitate a Winter Chemistry Carnival at the Digital Foundry in New KensingtonÂ for students in grades 3-6. Alumni Profile Laura Ward '05 '19 As the librarian at Fox Chapel Area High School, Point Park University alumna Laura Ward's hard work was recently recognized with theÂ Outstanding Pennsylvania School Library AwardÂ from the Pennsylvania School Library AssociationÂ (PSLA). Alumni Profile Orlandria Smith '16 '18 '23 \"The key benefit of Point Park's Psy.D. program is the quality of education. Before stepping out into the real world and seeing clients as a practicum student, I was well-prepared. I felt confident in myself and my skills and knew I could do amazing work with any client.\" Alumni Profile Emilee Fails '19 \"I chose Point Park because of its location in Downtown Pittsburgh. I knew Point Park had many connections within the sports industry and that it was in the ideal location to try and build a relationship with the local teams.\" Alumni Profile Kristin Serafini '15 \"Returning to the Pittsburgh Playhouse was incredibly special for me! Growing up doing theatre in Pittsburgh and training at Point Park shaped so much of who I am as both a performer and a person. Coming back to my roots for this show felt like a full-circle moment.\" 2024 Highlights Friday, December 27, 2024 From our acceptance into the NCAA to the inauguration of our ninth president, it was an eventful year for the Pioneers. Sports, Arts, Entertainment & Music Business Program Blends On-Campus Experiences, Real-World Opportunities to Prepare Students for a Dynamic Industry Monday, December 9, 2024 \"From learning the latest industry trends to working directly with experts and peers on impactful initiatives, the SAEM program equips you with the knowledge, adaptability and confidence needed to thrive in competitive fields. Itâs a launchpad for building meaningful careers in the dynamic worlds of sports, arts, entertainment and music.\" Alumni Profile Brendan McNamara '24 \"The B.A. in journalism prepared me for my career by providing hands-on experience through the student-run television station. That experience has all tied into my current position at WTRF-TV.\" Students in the Ph.D. in Community Engagement Program's New Cohort Reflect on the Start of a Transformative Journey Monday, October 28, 2024 \"I am most excited to experience the evolutions and expansions that will occur through this program. This Ph.D. journey wonât be an easy one, but I am not alone. Since the start of the program, I have been supported by my cohort members, professors and local community partnerships.\" Alumni Profile Erin Yudt '24 Alumnus Erin Yudt '24 details her experience in Fulbright Germany's Berlin Capital Program. Alumni Profile Jimyse Brown '22 \"The work that you do in the community engagement program is undoubtedly connected to what you want to do professionally. When you attack it with the best intentions in a genuine way and you dive in and give your all, you can be transformed and fully show up in the sector that you desire.\" Alumni Profile Todd Eagen '90 \"When I drive past Point Park's campus now, walk through the bookstore or visit the new Pittsburgh Playhouse, the University has really expanded, and itâs an even greater environment for students to learn, meet friends and have a good college experience.\" Alumni Profile Women Who Rock Concert Provides Alumna, Students with Meaningful Live Entertainment Experience \"Working with women who do not apologize for taking up space and who have a commitment to making a change in our society is something that the younger me would have never imagined I could achieve.\" Point SPARK: Entrepreneurship Camp 2024 Thursday, August 22, 2024 \"The camp definitely piqued my interest in being an entrepreneur one day. All the activities, all the things Iâve learned â they're topics and concepts I didnât know were so important. It's something Iâm keeping my mind on in the future.\"Â Alumni Profile Logan Hoffman '20 \"Business is the foundation of my role. The skills I gained in Point Park's business management program help me daily when speaking with businesses for stories and building my connections.\" Alumni Profile Megan Chiu '20 \"Point Park University has so much to offer. The facilities are amazing and the dance program prepares you for your career.\" Alumni Profile Lydia Grimenstein '20 \"The meaningful connections you make at Point Park have a real impact on your life. You'll find no better place than Pittsburgh to start your journey, whatever that may look like.\" Award-Winning Actor Jaquel Spivey '21 Reminds the Class of 2024, \"Be Loud and Proud That You Went to Point Park University\" Thursday, May 30, 2024 \"The world is still discovering who Point Park is and what Point Park is, and they don't know the beauty and excellence that is in this university. I hope you leave here today and you are loud and proud that you went to Point Park University.\" Pittsburgh Playhouse 2024-25 Season Monday, May 13, 2024 The Pittsburgh Playhouse is launching several new suites of programming including Arts Accelerator, which will connect Point Park students with professional alumni working on Broadway and beyond in the performing arts industry. Point Park University Celebrates 64th Commencement and Hooding Ceremonies Monday, April 29, 2024 Point Park University celebrated graduation at PPG Paints Arena on Friday, April 26. Alumni Profile Mark Bonacci '10 '23 \"I recommend Point Park with every fiber of my being. Point Park has helped me unlock doors that I believed to be previously unopenable. The School of Education has great faculty and staff!\" Alumni Profile Maggie Stasko '18 \"Iâve always felt so prepared for what I do professionally because of what I was taught at Point Park. Having professorsÂ who are still in the field makes all the difference because theyâre able to teach from experience. Itâs more real world and less textbook.\" Springboard Danse Relocates International Project to Point Park, Bringing World-Renowned Artists to Pittsburgh Tuesday, April 16, 2024 \"Our Department of Dance consistently ranks among the very best in the United States, so it makes sense to build a partnership with Springboard, which is recognized worldwide as a destination for career development.\" Alumni Profile Carlos Polanco '20 '21 \"Point Park's supportive faculty, diverse opportunities and vibrant campus community truly shaped my journey and prepared me for success in the sports industry.\" Alumni Profile Tyler Cook '20 \"Point Park finds the perfect balance of theory, application and real-world experience. The Ed.D. program is scaffolded in a way that develops your understanding of leadership theory and then empowers you to apply it to your everyday life in a practical and impactful way.\" Alumni Profile Jaquel Spivey '21 Point Park offered body diversity, ethnic diversity and equal training in acting, singing and dancing. Not many schools offer that, and thatâs what made it stand out to me. IÂ knew I would be welcomed and would have the opportunity to shine. 2023 Year in Review Wednesday, December 27, 2023 From electing a new president to charting a bold path forward to shape the University's future, Point Park is celebrating our highlights from 2023. Take a look back at some of our top stories of the year. Alumni Profile Mai Hassan '23 \"The ABCTE program supported my professional development and growth by offering an essential curriculum that covered fundamental concepts and delved into advanced topics.\" Students Network, Explore Music and Live Entertainment Industry at IEBA Conference in Nashville Tuesday, December 5, 2023 Students and faculty from the Sports, Arts, Entertainment & Music Business program traveled to Music City this semester to attend the sold-out International Entertainment Buyers Association Conference, a leading not-for-profit trade organization for live entertainment industry professionals. Alumni Profile Robert Michael, Ed.D., '23 \"Teaching is undoubtedly a challenging profession that has evolved significantly over the past decade. However, with proper preparation and unwavering dedication, it can be one of the most rewarding careers. Point Park University ensures that you have the essential tools for success.\" Criminal Justice, Intelligence & National Security and Behavioral Sciences Majors Intern, Work for Alumnus-Led Legal Consulting Nonprofit Friday, October 13, 2023 \"Contributing to The JASON Project's mission helps to give me a sense of satisfaction because I get to help truly make a difference in someone's life.\" Alumni Profile Brandon Moon '15 \"The SAEM program really did more for me than just provide a degree. It's real-life scenario-based learning, thanks to the professors who have actually lived and excelled in their respective industries.\" Alumni Profile Haley Gillespie '22 \"Having a degree in dance from Point Park has helped me earn respect from my colleagues. Graduating from the program says something about the kind of student you are, and the level of excellence you bring.\" Alumni Profile Kate Vandivier '09 \"I have many fond memories as a student. It was the first time in my training that I was surrounded by so many talented people all pursuing the same goal, that I found a sense of community and belonging as a budding artist.\" Alumni Profile John M. Storey Jr. '20 \"Point Park University is education-driven, student-committed and focused on real-world experience. In addition to providing a top-notch education, it is my experience that Point Park's faculty are dedicated to the continued development of great people.\" Alumni Profile Levi Donaldson Brown '19 '23 \"Point Park's ABCTE program uses a hands-on approach focused on real classroom experience and prepares future teachers for their first year of teaching by familiarizing them with tools and skills they will use and incorporate into their classes.\" Alumni Profile Nick Fearon '15 \"To be a dance major at Point Park means that you will work harder than you ever have before, but you will also be rewarded with incredible memories and friends that will be so unique to your experience. The dance program pushes your limits and sets you up for a successful career.\" Alumni Profile Josh Frketic '11 \"My broadcasting degree is more than a degree. If I only had the degree, then I would not be where I am today. It is really what the University provides more than anything, and that is an opportunity to do great things.\" Alumni Profile Ahmad Simmons '10 \"I am so lucky to have had the foundation of Point Park's dance training. It has allowed me to thrive in so many areas of the arts industry as a performer from state to screen â and now on the other side of the table.\" Alumni Profile Adelyn Biedenbach '12 \"Point Park's faculty has real-world experience. Most of my professors were still working in the industry and had real-life experiences to share in the classroom.\" Alumni Profile Monae Findley '20 '22 \"My decision to open my store was inspired by the deep sense of community at Point Park. The vibrant and diverse culture of the city, coupled with a personal connection to the community, made Pittsburgh the ideal location for a business centered around communal growth and sustainability.\" SAEM Alumni Thrive in Nashville Entertainment Industry Tuesday, August 1, 2023 \"I landed multiple internships and jobs throughout my career because of the connections I made and the opportunities I was given at Point Park.\" Alumni Profile John Spare '17 \"If you dream of being a screenwriter, it's imperative that you surround yourself with like-minded creatives. I was able to watch, learn and be involved in the work of my talented classmates, and that is something that can't be experienced writing in a room by yourself.\" Alumni Profile Aspen Mock '18 \"I would recommend Point Park University's Leadership and Administration program because it is an opportunity to empower lifelong learners along their leadership journeys, shaping their paths so they can make profound contributions in their fields.\" Alumni Profile Sherlyn Harrison '21 \"At Point Park, you do not have to sacrifice your life and work to complete a degree because Point Park promotes academic excellence while focusing on student needs.\" Alumni Profile Josh Croup '18 \"The hands-on training I received at Point Park from professors who are still working in the field gave me a strong foundation that helped me hit the ground running as soon as I graduated.\" Alumni Profile Josh McCann '18 '23 \"Point Park is known for having a culturally rich and diverse creative community. I knew deep down that this was the place for me. The location in the city is inspiring, the professors are amazing and the atmosphere is really cool.\" Alumni Profile E. Clayton Cornelious Broadway actor E. Clayton Cornelious played the role of Paul Williams in the first National Tour of Ain't Too Proud - The Life and Times of The Temptations. Cornelious is also a co-producer of the Broadway hit new musical New York, New York. Alumni Profile Cody Risch '22 \"Point Park University is affordable and offers in-person and online courses. This gives you the flexibility to complete your degree how you prefer. Point Park is always evaluating its curriculum and adding new classes that offer real-world expertise.\" Alumni Profile Luis Mujica '22 \"Point Park goes further than just providing education. Faculty and staff take into consideration that you are a human being, and the campus culture makes it clear that every student will be supported throughout their journey regardless of their life situation.\"Â Alumni Profile Shyanne Rippole '21 \"All of Point Park's School of Education professors â and I mean all of them â will help you map out the way. They are so knowledgeable and know so many different people in the field to help you make connections. The School of Education is its own family.\" Alumni Profile Lauryn Nania '21 \"The faculty have real-life newsroom experience to help guide aspiring journalists. My assignments immersed me into the experience of being a reporter outside of an academic environment.\" Alumni Profile Caroline Collins '15 '19 \"I learned that being authentic, staying up-to-date on the ever-changing platforms and consistency was key in building and maintaining an engaged following. I owe a lot of my social media success to all that I learned in graduate school at Point Park University.\" Alumni Profile Phillip Gertz '16 \"Point Park prepared me for my career by allowing me to focus on truly learning and applying course concepts instead of just answering questions on a test.\" Chandler Krelow '20 Tuesday, May 2, 2023 \"For young intelligence professionals, many eyes are locked in on three-letter agencies for their first job. While this is a fantastic career choice, intelligence is everywhere. There are career opportunities at banks, universities, corporations and so much more.\" Alumni Profile Jade Steele-Stripsky '21 \"If a student wants to gain real-world experience in urban education and first-hand knowledge from professors who have dedicated their lives to education and preparing future teachers, Point Park's School of Education is where they want to be.\" SAEM 20th Anniversary Celebration Friday, April 14, 2023 \"It's not just learning from a book. It's always been about adaptability and learning new skill sets. That mentality is something I take into my job now. I love that I have a degree in SAEM from Point Park and I'm proud to be an alumna.\" Alumni Profile Viveca Chow '16 \"I had an incredible support system from all my friends and teachers. The teachers really care about you and your individuality at Point Park, and that's what I loved the most.\" Alumni Profile Sri Vemulapalli '16 \"I highly recommend Point Park based on its reputation, curriculum and collaborative environment. Upon walking through the door, I experienced a positive atmosphere, a diverse student body and a welcoming attitude.\" Alumni Profile Mallory Marinack '12 \"Take classes in all styles, not just your concentration, and take a variety of teachers. Every teacher has a different array of knowledge and insight into the dance world that can prove to be invaluable in shaping your future.\" Alumni Profile Zoey Angelucci '22 \"I found my internships and freelance experience to be the most rewarding and valuable parts of my time at Point Park. If it weren't for these experiences, I probably wouldn't be in this position and would feel behind in the professional world.\" Alumni Profile Alumnus James Gowan and Fellow Alonzo King LINES Ballet Company Members Host Q&A with Students \"Point Park's rigorous dance program provides students the ability to grow and have a taste of the real world before they step into it. Additionally, the diverse program allows students to explore all that dance can be.\" Alumni Profile Lindsey Ramsey '13 '14 \"I recommend Point Parkâs School of Education because the department embodies what they teach. When you enroll, you see diversity amongst your peers. You are offered inclusive learning opportunities tailored to your needs. You are given opportunities to participate in programs and activities that support your personal and professional growth. Point Park is truly an environment where everyone can thrive!\" Alumni Profile Tony Moux '13 \"Since graduating, I have been published nationally in editorial magazines, photographed and creatively directed campaigns for brands like Dermalogica, PPG Paints and People Magazine. I've had so many opportunities that I was able to build from my college experience.\" Alumni Profile Annie Gagen '15 \"At the time I was looking at schools, Point Park was one of the few that offered a concentration in jazz, rather than just ballet and modern. That was one of the first things that drew me there, aside from the excellent reputation that both the dance and musical theatre departments had.\" Alumni Profile Melissa Botta-Havran '22 \"The faculty and staff in Point Park's School of Education have their finger on the pulse of what is most challenging in education today.Â They are knowledgeable and incredibly accessible, which, as a working mom, was important to me as I navigated this program.\" Alumni Profile Aaron Myler '16 \"Point Park prepared me for my career by giving me a realistic look into the TV industry. The classes were led byÂ industry professionals and treated like the first leg of your career. I learned every role that plays a part in putting a newscast together.\" Alumni Profile Ashley C. Stokes '18 \"Having four regional Emmyâs under my belt after my first year working for PBS is humbling. It inspires me to continue to share stories that make a difference in our communities and eventually around the world.\" Alumni Profile Reyna Guerra '20 \"The Conservatory of Performing Arts is known for its rigorous training. I knew of the solid reputation of its graduates and felt it was the place to grow as an artist and learn more about the industry.\" Alumni Profile Caitlin Dee '17 \"The drive I developed during college to try new things and explore different places has really helped me during this experience, but the support I received from School of Education professors encouraging me and telling me to challenge myself has been immensely impactful throughout my career. I learned I can do difficult things, and Point Park helped me build that confidence.\" Alumni Profile Tracy Brigden '19 \"I've plays performed around the country, a podcast reach number one on the charts and a film script in development with a major production company. I would have never thought I could do all that without the learning and encouragement from Point Park University's M.F.A. program.\" Alumni Profile Milky Tran '20 \"I loved that you began making and experimenting with film your freshman year ... Iâm grateful that Point Park had such a heavy focus on storytelling and allowed me to go through the full process of making a film many, many times.\" Alumni Profile Hunter Mikles '16 Jazz alumnus Hunter Mikles '16 authored \"Hunter the Dancing Fox\" to inspire young artists to pursue their dreams. Alumni Profile Christina BeltrÃ¡n Revilla '15 \"While pursuing my MBA degree, I participated in an internship at an international company while working three jobs to support myself. Point Park allowed me to take classes around my busy schedule, which was incredible.\" Alumni Profile Tianna Davis '22 \"Most, if not everything I learned at Point Park helped me become the artist I am today. I took everything that I learned from the wonderful faculty, and I ingrained it into all of the work I perform and create.\" 2022 Fall High School Media Day Thursday, October 27, 2022 More than 160 prospective students explored the fields of media, marketing and communication at Point Park University's annual High School Media Day Oct. 21. Alumni Profile Justin Stengel '21 \"I would recommend Point Park to a prospective student because of its distinctive learning opportunities. Point Parkâs small class sizes and experienced professors set you up with a unique chance to gain an excellent comprehension of your field before you even begin your career. By choosing Point Park, you set yourself up to be successful in your chosen field.\" Alumni Profile Jana Larell Glover '22 \"I had the best time auditioning for SIX. As an alternate, I cover three of the six queens and use so many skills I developed in college. This show was beautifully written, composed and choreographed, and as an actor, it is my job to portray that the best I can.\" Alumni Profile Caleb Mathura '22 2022 musical theatre alumnus Caleb Mathura plays Kevin G. in MEAN GIRLS the Musical. Alumni Profile Andrea Weinzierl '14 \"I chose Point Park because of how well-rounded the Conservatory is. I knew I would get top-notch training in all three disciplines: singing, dancing and acting.\" Alumni Profile Tanika Harris '22 \"Degree programs at Point Park University have been designed with the adult learner in mind. The accelerated and 4+1 programs guarantee that students are adequately equipped to enter a developing and changing workforce.\" Alumni Profile Melessie Clark '15 \"Point Park equipped me with the confidence, materials and skills needed to not only have a successful audition, but it also prepared me for what is required once a role is obtained,\" said Clark. Point Park University's Latest Para2Teacher Cohort Celebrates 100% Completion Monday, July 25, 2022 \"I benefited from the Para2Teacher program immediately. Right away, I was able to adjust the way I teach and started collaborating with my peers to better serve our students. I now have the tools to be a highly-effective educator thanks to the coursework and hands-on student practicum experience.\" Alumni Profile Erin Carlin '14 Meet alumna Erin Carlin, M.A., manager, PR and corporate communications, St. Clair Health. Alumni Profile Craig Johnston '21 \"Point Park offers an effective, efficient teaching certificate program. The School of Education faculty are supportive and honest.Â The feedback I received from the faculty helped me grow professionally and personally. The program offers flexibility and the resources needed to obtain a teaching certificate in a short period of time.\" Criminal Justice Alumnus Gets Assist from Point Park UniversityÂ in Helping Improve Legal Outcomes for People in Need Wednesday, July 20, 2022 The JASON Project, a nonprofit that supports people in need of assistance navigating the court system, is preparing â with support from Point Park University â to make its services more widely available to Pittsburgh-area residents. Alumni Profile Jessica (Szramowski) Monahan '10 \"Point Park provided a multitude of hands-on experiences, intimate class settings and guidance from faculty with exceptional backgrounds in their respective fields. Point Park showed me what could be possible and provided the tools to achieve it.\" Alumni Profile Arian Clay-Sirop '09 \"My broadcasting classes prepared me for the industry I work in today. I endured the hustle of racing around Pittsburgh with a camera in my hand trying to capture a story, then spent hours in the edit suites editing the footage.\" B.F.A. in Photography Program Emphasizes Pre-Professional Skills Wednesday, July 13, 2022 \"Point Park is the only University in Downtown Pittsburgh offering a B.F.A. in Photography.  Students begin with a tool-based foundation learning cameras, imaging programs and outputs, followed by two years of research, production and refinement.\" Alumni Profile Max Kovalchuk '14 \"All of my professors had a positive impact on me. In particular, I reached out to Professor Traversari when I was in high school to schedule time to talk about the music business. That conversation ultimately led to my decision to attend Point Park.\" Alumni Profile Gregory Porter '13 '20 \"Point Park's urban campus setting is beautiful and full of opportunity. The classes are affordable and a great value. The online learning platforms are easy to use and follow. The professors are dedicated to seeing you succeed.\" Alumni Profile Connor Russell '12 \"Point Park gave me the tools I needed to gain a well-rounded foundation in the arts. I left my college experience feeling like I had a solid footing in every area that I studied. In my opinion, this flexibility has greatly impacted my post-college career.\" Alumni Profile Stephanie Kyung Sun Walters '22 \"For a working professional who doesnât want to uproot their entire life/family, this program is a great fit ... The educators are here to help you succeed when experiencing new mediums or tackling a different format.\" Point Park University Graduates Nicole Bon and Jerome Mathews Named Exemplary Student Teachers by Pittsburgh's School District University Collaborative Tuesday, June 14, 2022 \"My student teaching experience reaffirmed that I am meant to teach and that I have chosen the right path for myself. Every day I worked extremely hard to make sure my students' needs were being met and that I was listening, watching and applying all the advice that my cooperating teachers gave me to help me improve and better myself as a future educator.\" Alumni Profile Alexandra Barr '20 \"The diverse and artistic approach that the School of Education applies to teaching is outstanding and assures students that they will be prepared for the field. The field experiences I accumulated during my Point Park career provided me with different strategies that can be used globally.\" Alumni Profile Travis Johnston '15 \"The SAEM program is an excellent fit for students who wish to learn by doing.\" Alumni Profile Dana Bohince '16 \"The multimedia program provided me with a number of courses that I could build hard and soft skills around. The Downtown location, coupled with dedicated professors, meant that I was frequently introduced to industry professionals from media outlets across the city.\" Alumni Profile Christine Schell '15 \"The SAEM program preparedÂ me for success by incorporating internships into the curriculum my junior and senior year.\" Alumni Profile Maeve Gallagher '13 \"Coaching and teaching at the collegiate level is a dream of a career, and I believe Point Park gave me the foundation for both.Â TheÂ School of Education put such an emphasis on experiential learning and that preparation was immeasurably beneficial in my development as an educator. Learning from faculty who have real-world experience in the field was also a major benefit.\" Alumni Profile Nicole Merrick '16 '17 and Bernie Merrick '18 \"There is so much value in Point Parkâs criminal justice and intelligence programs. The subject matter is comprehensive, relevant and captivating. The faculty have a wide range of career backgrounds, from working in field operations to being highly-educated scholars.\" Alumni Profile Diamonte Walker '22 \"Point Park has its finger on the pulse of what is needed to shape the leaders and practitioners who are shaping tomorrow.\" Alumni, Published Authors Reflect on Value of Point Park University's Creative Writing Program Tuesday, April 19, 2022 \"If it werenât for the creative inspirations of Professor GirmanÂ and Karen Dwyer, Ph.D., I would not be where I am now. I give all my thanks to these wonderful professors.Â Point Park constantly encourages students to find their potential. This school is more than a place to gain a degree â itâs home.\" Alumni Profile Joseph Kozarian '15 '22 \"I think what sets a degree from Point Park apart from other universities is that the professors have decades of practical experience in criminal justice fields. Additionally, Point Park offers smaller class sizes and professors truly get to know each student.\" Alumni Profile Matthew Uzar '20 \"Point Parkâs nontraditional campus atmosphere in Downtown Pittsburgh is truly its greatest strength. The urban location places students within walking distance of nearly every major entertainment venue in the city.\" Alumni Profile Erica Roney '16 \"Point Parkâs program provided me with the flexibility to learn about different areas within the world of business management. At the time, I didnât know what would spark my interest, but the wide variety of classes â from marketing to human resourcesÂ â armed me with a skillset that I could bring to any role, including communications.\" Alumni Profile Amanda Ardinger '13 \"Point Park gave me the opportunity to be a student, an athlete, a friend, leader and young professional all at the same time. The professors at Point Park are knowledgeable and friendly. I felt that the education that I received in the classroom prepared me for my future career and gave me the confidence I needed to run my own classroom.\" Oyster Creative Co. is Home to Point Park Alumni and a Professor Thursday, March 17, 2022 \"I am proud of the work we've been doing at Oyster and the tremendous relationship we've been able to cultivate with Point Park,\" saidÂ Jenna Lo Castro, Ph.D., assistant professor and director of communications and strategy at Oyster.Â Alumni Profile Royce Jones '20 \"Point Park supplied me with the tools I needed to achieve success. The small class sizes really opened the door for a lot of one-on-one critique and feedback from professors, many of whom are absolutely outstanding in their respective crafts with expansive resumes and career experience.\" Alumni Profile Meghna Banerjee '21 \"I will always recommend Point Park because of its diverse culture and competitive education pattern, which enables students like me to feel confident and ready for professional career growth.\" Student Profile Brianna Kamauf â22 \"Working with M Chancey Management has helped me narrow down my goals and focus on building concrete skills.Â I have learned to take chances on myself and to be confident in my skills and adaptability to new environments. The music industry is constantly growing and changing, and I have learned how to grow with it from the hands-on experience I have gained.\" Alumni Profile Lamont Walker II '17 \"Teachers like Zeva Barzell, Robin Walsh, and so many others I was fortunate to work with, knew how to shape young actors who had a passion for their craft. Point Park taught me how to do the hard work and I was blessed to have professors who shaped the actor I am today.\" Alumna and Student Pass National Public Relations Exam Friday, February 11, 2022 Stacey FederoffÂ '21 and Meghan MacioceÂ '19 '22 recently passed the Certificate in Principles of Public Relations exam from the Public Relations Society of America (PRSA). Alumni Profile Autumn Turk '20 \"Through my coursework and learning experiences at Point Park, I learned the importance of understanding adult learning and that we as leaders need to be mindful of adult learning theory when designing professional development for our teachers.\" Alumni Profile Greg Fedor '21 \"I would recommend Point Park because having Downtown Pittsburgh as your campus is unlike any other college experience. The location allows the University to foster great connections with businesses and organizations that hold significant value for students starting their careers.\" Alumni Profile Prim Green '19 '21 \"My broadcasting and MBA classes were very informative. Everything I learned in class, I can tie back to my position. Roll-out schedules, digital and social media calendars, marketing toolkits and entertainment law material are all subjects I learned in the classroom.\" Alumni Profile Giuseppe Esposito '19 \"One of the reasons I chose Point Park was its location. It was hard to beat for me. The equipment and facilitiesÂ for the animation program are top-notch as well, so make use of it all.\" Alumni Profile Allison Schubert '20 \"My internships and the hands-on experience prepared me, and nearly all of my employers have been impressed with how much experience I gained just through being involved.\" Alumni Profile Sucharitha Donepudi '21 \"The MSISBA program at Point Park introduces data science and analytics concepts and provides a good pathway for new graduates to find oneâs own career path, be it as a data analyst, data scientist or data specialist in the domain of their choice.\" Alumni Profile Brianna Wuenschel '20 \"The program's immediate immersion in filmmaking was so different from other schools. From the first year you are already creating your own films and this was very important to me in choosing a school.\" Alumni Profile Jordyn Hronec '21 Pittsburgh Business Times hires 2021 School of Communication grad Jordyn Hronec as a digital producer. Alumni Profile Maya Bowles '20 \"The faculty prepared us for the professional world through mock auditions, having talk-backs with artists and learning/being evaluated by current choreographers in the industry. I began auditioning in New York my senior year and was so surprised by how prepared I felt in the room.\" Alumni Profile Kaylin Horgan '11 Point Park dance alumna Kaylin Horgan's work Milton was named Best Virtual Stage Production of 2021 by Pittsburgh City Paper. Alumni Profile Teresa Rodgers '20 \"The best thing about the Global Cultural Studies program is that it showed me the real-world perspective. It is mind-opening and answers questions you never thought you could have theorized. It makes you think and truly look at nations, institutions, news and people through different lenses.\" Alumni Profile Brian Kutchak '19 \"My doctoral degree in educational leadership from Point Park University has made me a more well-rounded leader. To build leadership capacity among staff members, I would often use and share passages and articles directly from my coursework with my staff.\" 2021 Golden Quill Awards Monday, October 11, 2021 Point Park University students, alumni and faculty were honored at the Press Club of Western Pennsylvania's 57th annual Golden Quill Awards, held Sept. 28 at the Rivers Casino. Alumni Q&A: Deborah Skillings-Phillips, Ph.D., and Karen Smoot, Ed.D. Monday, October 4, 2021 Sisters Deborah Skillings-Phillips and Karen Smoot leaned on each other for support as they successfully defended their doctoral dissertations in September, earning a Ph.D. in Community Engagement and Ed.D. in Leadership and Administration, respectively. Alumni Profile Jeff Gorti '16 \"The training I had at Point Park's Conservatory of Performing Arts prepared me for the rigor of real life ... Also, the facilities that you get to train, rehearse and perform in are absolutely incredible. It is truly top of the line.\" Alumni Profile Noelle Novakovich '15 \"I left my undergrad with so many transferable skills. The small class sizes made it easier to learn, ask questions and be more hands-on. I felt confident and ready to take the next step into the working world and I have many Point Park professors to thank for that.\" Alumni Profile Dara Schlesinger '21 \"Point Park University has an amazing dance program. I'm so glad I made the investment to learn and train at one of the top dance programs in the country.\" Alumni Profile Sara (Cumpston) Jeffries '20 \"Education is not always the easiest job, but the outcome of it is always beautiful. If I can inspire one student like some of my Point Park professors have inspired me, then I have reached my goal as an educator.\" Alumni Profile Nicole Paladin '12 \"I really appreciated the push from faculty to gain real-world experience while in school. The classes frequently set up events, even outside of the campus, where the class had to create and pitch products along with an advertising plan.\" Alumni Profile Ashley Arnold '21 \"The faculty and staff at Point Park are with you each step of the way and are always there to assist you with any questions or needs that may arise. The camaraderie with your peers and cohort within the program is immeasurable and very beneficial as you go through the program together.\" Alumni Profile Jennifer Taormina-Lawson '13 \"The classes and faculty at Point Park still impact my work to this day. I interned at Sony Music Entertainment and SAG-AFTRA while in law school, and I know that I was awarded those opportunities because of my undergraduate education and experience. There is no doubt about that.\" Professional Career-Readiness Center 2020-21 Annual Report Tuesday, August 31, 2021 Boosting student professional skills, connecting to meaningful employment and collaborating to implement workforce solutions are just a few achievements reported in the 2020-21 Annual Report for of Point Park Universityâs Professional Career-Readiness Center. Alumni Profile Mitchell Roell '21 \"Point Park was the best option for me. They had electrical engineering, which I wanted to study all during high school, and they had a lot more to offer. Since I lived in the Pittsburgh area, I was able to commute while also continuing to work part time. I was also able to play soccer against some of the best teams at the college level. Both of my parents are Point Park alumni, and, for me, it was an easy decision.\" Alumni Profile Robert Trinkle '12 \"My education was the catalyst that enabled me to transition seamlesslyÂ into the post-graduate world. Having an established relationship through networking made the transition to PNC seamless for me.\" Alumni Profile Veronika Panagiotou '21 Ph.D. in community engagement alumna Veronika Panagiotou is an advocacy and program manager for the National Coalition for Cancer Survivorship. Alumni Profile Julio SepÃºlveda '18 \"Point Park has a very special campus in Downtown Pittsburgh, and the location allows its students to explore jobs or internship opportunities all around the city.\" Alumni Profile Amrita Chakraborti '21 \"Balancing a full-time position, a graduate program and a toddler can be really challenging and overwhelming at times, but Point Park has made it possible. Point Park'sÂ locationÂ drew me towards choosing the University for my MBA program.\" Alumni Profile Steven Reed '19 \"Going to school in Downtown Pittsburgh was one of the main reasons I chose to come to Point Park. The campus location connects students to the best of what Pittsburgh has to offer. Not only are we minutes from Market Square and Point State Park, but there are many hidden gems in terms of restaurants and attractions just a short walk from Point Park's campus.\" Alumni Profile Colin Jacob '15 \"Point Park provided the space for me to grow on a technical level, and I also honed my artistic expression in dance. I came out of the program with an understanding of different styles of movement and the way to put myself into them.\" Alumni Profile Livia Rice '16 \"I graduated from Point Park with several job offers. Point Park truly prepares you for your future career and will help you discover your passion. The Downtown Pittsburgh location is also unmatched.\" Alumni Profile Karly Shorts '13 \"Point Parkâs behavioral sciences program prepared me for my career by introducing me to counseling skills at the undergraduate level, as well as introducing me to the concept of trauma. I remember vividly having to audio record 'practice' counseling sessions with fellow classmates, and this helped me develop my skills for reflection and showed me that being a therapist was exactly where I wanted to be.\" Alumni Profile John Blattenberger '19 \"Say yes to any and every opportunity. You never know where it may lead you. Make connections with as many people in your desired industry as you possibly can. This starts by connecting with your professors. Sit in the front of your classes and always ask questions. You or your parents are investing a lot in you. Get your, or their, moneyâs worth.\" Alumni Profile Nicole Lakovic '21 \"The SAEM faculty are so knowledgeableÂ and have great industry experience to share. One of my favorite things was listening to their real-world stories. The coursework was all relevant, and I use skills that Iâve learned in classes in my job every day!\" Student Profile Rachel Hienz '90 '21 A 2021 Distinguished Alumni awardee, Rachel Hienz is a full-time instructor at the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers Local Union #5Â Joint Apprenticeship Training Center. She will complete her master's degree in Adult Learning and Training this summer. Alumni Profile Nathan Gentry '19 M.A. in media communication grad's photography exhibitions have been featured across the United States and abroad. Alumni Profile Kim Roberts '15 \"The coursework and faculty did an incredible job of preparing me for my career. The classes taught me all of the essential skills, from AP Style to Photoshop, which prepared me for the internships that led to my first full-time job.\" Alumni Profile Carol Mullen '18 \"If you're looking for a program that prepares you to do your best writing, challenges you to work hard and continue to get better, this is the right creative home for you.\" Alumni Profile Taleesha Johnson '14 \"Knowing that I am a part of the bigger process that is helping to do good by the city in which I have always lived makes me proud to come to work every day.\" Intelligence and National Security Studies Grad Shares Career Advice and Benefits of a Point Park Education Friday, June 18, 2021 Speaking under the condition of anonymity due to the nature of their job, a 2019 alum now working as an intelligence specialist with the U.S. intelligence community shares their Point Park experience. Alumni Profile Hannah (Frye) Bridge '12 \"The size of Point Park was a huge benefit. It allowed me one-on-one time with faculty, where I got to know my professors and they got to know me. The organizations and on-campus programs acted as mini-internships where I could use my skills outside of the classroom.\" Alumni Profile Carly Lutz '21 \"My dreams are big, and my heart is kind. I have no doubt that I will change the field of education in some capacity.\" Alumni Profile Meghan Sexton '06 '10 Point Park alumna Meghan Sexton helps oversee roadway, traffic and geotechnical engineering and design projects for the Allegheny County Department of Public Works. Alumni Profile Sharimar Y. Cruz '18 \"I had very little knowledge of the art world when I applied to Point Park. I began my journey with an interest in photography and Point Park helped turn it into my passion. The B.F.A. program provided me with the knowledge I needed to succeed in this industry.\" Alumni Profile Kevin Squires '19 \"The opportunities for learning outside of a traditional, lecture-based, brick-and-mortar setting were incredibly valuable. Field observations, class trips and meeting with teachers and principals were additional elements that made the content connect with the real world.\" Alumni Profile Sean McKeag '14 Alumnus Sean McKeag received nine Pennsylvania Newspaper Awards for his work as a photojournalist. Alumni Profile Dustin Wolf '18 \"Point Parkâs dance program is unlike anything else. The faculty are phenomenal and give their all to help fulfill every studentâs potential. I would not be the dancer or person I am today without them and for that I am so thankful.\" Alumni Profile Maria Montaro '20 Ph.D. in community engagement alumna named a 30 Under 30 honoree by the Pittsburgh Business Times. Trio of School of Education Alumni Work Together at The Campus Laboratory of Carlow University Thursday, May 13, 2021 At the Campus Laboratory School of Carlow University, Point Park University alumni Kayla Posney, Valerie Patilla and Laurie Laird are applying their passion for teaching to foster hands-on, creative learning opportunities for pre-K students.Â Alumni Profile Kristin (Snapp) Andreassi '17 \"I knew the professors still worked in the industry at the area's top publications, leading to relevant course material and meaningful connections. Point Park's location in the city also sets students up for seemingly endless internship and post-grad job opportunities.\" Pathways to Perform Podcast Tuesday, April 27, 2021 Dance Professor Kiesha Lalama teamed up with School of Communication students to produce the Pathways to Perform podcast. The goal of the podcast is to inspire and guide young artists on a path towards success in various industries. Alumni Profile Logan Smith '20 \"The experience gained during my time at Point Park is unmatched. Each course is curated to offer the highest quality of education that is available. On top of that, the professors remain in contact with important individuals within the industry to add an extra level of immersion into each course.\" Alumni Profile Colten Gill '17 \"The emphasis on professional development and career exploration is really something that sets Point Park apart. Especially in the Rowland School of Business, the focus on every step of your career process â from how to apply to internships to negotiating your salary, becoming a supervisor and more â while also gaining the functional skills in your concentration was incredibly helpful.\" Alumni Profile Lin Sun '13 \"The SAEM faculty teach you the importance of hands-on experience, and I cannot stress enough how true that is! It's a very competitive industry so you have to do whatever it takes for your resume to stand out.\" Alumni Profile Sophia Duff '19 SAEM alumna Sophia Duff works at OMG23, an advertising agency contracted by Disney to handle their in-house media planning. Alumni Profile Kimberly Keagy '19 \"With the hands-on experience in the classroom from day one, I was prepared for internships my sophomore year of college. Do as many internships as possible, the more real-world experience you have will help you excel.\" Alumni Profile Kimie Parker '19 \"Point Parkâs dance facilities are an absolute luxury. I donât think Iâll have many opportunities to be in studios as expansive or advanced as Point Parkâs for the rest of my career.\" Alumni Profile Malaki Davis '20 \"I really enjoyed the Point Park campus environment. I liked the small, interactive classes and learning from professors who have experience working in the industry. It is a great school filled with prestigious faculty and a talented student body. Point Park gives you opportunities.\" Alumni Profile Michael Cruse '20 \"At Point Park, I learned how to manage multiple projects, conduct research and analyze data, utilize history to assist in making decisions and a great deal about the criminal justice system in Pennsylvania.\" Alumni Profile Emily VanderMey '20 \"Point Park is at the center of everything. There's never a shortage of internships, volunteering or career events. Every professor was kind and generous, whether they were meeting with me, referring me to potential clients or giving support as I was applying to grad programs.\" Alumni Profile Emily Bezak '10 \"I learned through doing at Point Park, and from faculty and staff with work experience in their chosen fields. When I went to business school and climbed the corporate ladder afterward, I quickly realized my leg up on the other students and my colleagues. I worked in groups on real-world problems for years already, thanks to the experience I had at Point Park.\" Alumni Profile Hannah Altman '17 \"The location in Downtown Pittsburgh was monumental for me as a student; as soon as I exited the classroom, I was in a city that felt big enough to grow into and small enough that meeting new people and seeing galleries was always an accessible opportunity.\" Alumni Profile Mara Meyer '20 \"If it weren't for Point Park's amazing professors, especially in the SAEM program, I donât believe I would be on the path I am today. They are the most supportive group of people that truly want to help you reach your full potential and push you to succeed. Their classes taught me necessary skills to build my own brand.\" Alumni Profile Benjamin Mapp '07 Benajamin Mapp received the Audelco Award, following in the footsteps of Denzel Washington, Viola Davis and the Late Chadwick Boseman, among others. Alumni Profile Lauren Clouser '20 \"At Point Park, many professors are still working in their fields and are able to provide up-to-date information about the industry and help us make important connections. I was also so excited to get to study in a city where so many opportunities are just a bus ride away.\" Alumni Profile Lydia Grimenstein '20 \"What drew me instantly to Point Park were its downtown location and ties to surrounding arts organizations. The SAEM program teaches you the fundamentals of business, but they also allow you to use what youâve learned to branch out into a field that interests you.\" Alumni Profile Courtney Blocher '20 \"The School of Education faculty and coursework provided me with a variety of teaching experiences in many different school settings. Throughout my classes, I was able to teach and observe in urban, suburban, private and center schools.Â Also, hearing about each of my professors' teaching experiences and watching how they taught helped me find my own style of teaching.\" Alumni Profile Nicholas Moran '15 \"Point Parkâs psychology department had a heavy emphasis on humanistic psychological perspectives, which continues to shape the way in which I approach my clinical work. I believe that my clients are the experts, and I am a helpful resource to assist with the co-construction of their fully actualized self. Point Park gave me necessary experience in conducting psychological research, presenting at conferences and improving my academic writing skills. I seek to provide an inclusive and brave space for my clients to explore all aspects of themselves and the intersections of their identities and presenting mental health concerns. Point Park helped me to see the client first as opposed to focusing on diagnosis.\" Alumni Profile Kara Sayers '20 \"Point Park gave me resources to succeed in whatever career path I chose, such as networking events, career fairs and a variety of class options. I felt prepared to dive into life after college.\" Alumni Profile Grace Offerdahl '20 \"Point Park and the SAEM program are so hands-on. It really is experiential learning, which makes learning so much more interesting. From internships to the shadowing program in SAEM 101, they really try to get you as much actual experience as possible, so you feel more prepared when you graduate. Also, the location is great, being right in the middle of the city. I liked that I wasnât separated from the city by a traditional campus, where every building around you is part of the school. I liked that I could walk outside of my dorm in Lawrence Hall and be right in the middle of it all.\" Alumni Profile Theresa Sowinski '17 Alumna Theresa Sowinski is an internal audit manager at PNC Bank. Alumni Profile Mina Hoffman '18 \"The most valuable thing Point Park gave me was a supportive network of people ... Additionally, having the hands-on filmmaking experience was priceless. Knowing set etiquette and general production speak is invaluable even in my role as a marketer.\" Point Park Alumni and Student are Building Their Careers at IMS Systems Monday, January 11, 2021 Point Park University alumni Edberg Dominguez, Angel Melendez and current student Joshua Jackson work for IMS Systems, a manufacturer of measurement solutions for steel and aluminum mills. Student Profile Ashley Bobak '22 Ashley Bobak, who earned a B.A. in psychology from Point Park University in 2013, is a doctoral candidate, part-time professor and therapist in the University Counseling Center. Students and Alumni Receive Robert L. Vann Media Awards from the Pittsburgh Black Media Federation Tuesday, January 5, 2021 Students and alumni are among the recipients of the 2020 Robert L. Vann Media Awards from the Pittsburgh Black Media Federation. The awards recognize outstanding journalism coverage of African American and African diaspora communities, individuals and issues.Â Katherine Schuler '15 Friday, December 18, 2020 Alumna Katherine Schuler is the founder and CEO of Rolling Pepperoni, a social enterprise business that sells pepperoni rolls retail, wholesale and ships nationwide. SAEM Virtual Sports Internship Thursday, December 17, 2020 The COVID-19 pandemic altered the internship landscape for Sports, Arts & Entertainment Management students seeking sports industry experience this fall. Through leveraging connections within the industry, Assistant Professor Robert Derda, M.S., launched the Virtual Sports Internship program. Alumni Profile Tejiri Odjighoro '19 Tejiri Odjighoro, who earned an M.S. in engineering management at Point Park, is a global engineering leader at Unilever. Alumni Profile Mira Patel '19 Mira Patel, who completed her MBA at Point Park, is now a medical student at Geisinger Commonwealth School of Medicine. Alumni Profile Bridget Benjamin '10 M.A. degree contributes to career success for alumna working for Scholastic, Rachel Ray Show, Watch What Happens Live and the Clinton Foundation. Alumni Profile James (Washington) Manning '11 \"The COPA schedule and rigor allowed me to feel prepared to enter the professional field; the versatility and class offerings played a huge part in that. As a student, you are treated and training like a professional dancer.\" Alumni Profile Adam Valen '15 Adam Valen is marketing manager for Drusky Entertainment and the Pennsylvania precinct captain for the National Independent Venue Association. Alumni Profile Rianne Lindsey '20 Theatre production alumna Rianne Lindsey '20 received the Altman Lighting Award for her work on Good Grief at the Pittsburgh Playhouse. Alumni Profile Kayla Snyder '20 \"From my first day at Point Park, we were learning real-world knowledge about the industry. The emphasis of experiential learning allowed me to complete five internships. The professors taught us everything according to industry standards, which prepared me greatly for my first job.\" Student Profile Shannon Gregg '14, '20 Shannon J. Gregg, Ph.D. in community engagement student, MBA grad and a part-time instructor, was recognized as a top influential woman in technology. Alumni Profile Amanda (King) Finkenbinder '12 \"My hands-on courses and internships allowed me to gain skills that the communications industry covets. Also, being able to walk downtown from my internships at KDKA-TV and the Pittsburgh Post-Gazette to my courses at Point Park was so convenient. The city was our playground for learning.\" Pittsburgh Rapper Wins Rowland School of Business' Vigor, Vibe and Venture Contest Thursday, November 12, 2020 The $10,000 prize will support Homewood native Yusef Sheltonâs message to bring positivity and empowerment to young, Black men. Alumni Profile Alyssa Briddes '16 \"Due to the hands-on nature of the program, we all learned on-set etiquette our first year, not just through our professors but through our upperclassmen. Learning how to behave on a set from Point Park has been invaluable during my time here in New York City.\" Alumni Profile Matt Desmond '12 \"I had opportunities to attend other universities out of high school, but what made Point Parkâs School of Communication stand out was the ability to get that hands-on experience from day one. You donât get that experience anywhere else.\" Point Park University Students, Alumni and Faculty Honored at Golden Quill Awards Thursday, September 17, 2020 Point Park University students, alumni and faculty earned top honors at the Press Club of Western Pennsylvania's 56th annual Golden Quill Awards, held virtually Sept. 3. Dance Department Hosts Virtual Speaker Series Friday, September 4, 2020 Each Monday, from Sept. 7 through Nov. 30 from 4:30 - 6:00 p.m., Point Park dance alumni and guest professionals will have engaging, virtual discussions organized into five categories: Broadway, Concert Dance, Choreographers, Entrepreneurs and the Commercial Dance Industry. Join us! Alumni Profile Taylor Fareri '13 Alumna Taylor Fareri '13 was nominated for her second Emmy award as a television news producer. Alumni Profile Corporal Aaron J. Allen '14 Meet Corporal Aaron J. Allen, a criminal justice administration alumnus of Point Park University and heritage liaison affairs officer for the Pennsylvania State Police. Spencer Marnich '20 Tuesday, August 25, 2020 Aware of the financial struggles many families face, Point Park University Pre-K through fourth grade elementary education graduate Spencer Marnich â20, decided to launch an annual Get Ready for School event to provide 100 new backpacks to school-aged children for free. Alumni Profile Gulcan Tokluoglu, Ed.D., '15 Gulcan Tokluoglu, a 2015 MBA alumna who concentrated in international business, was recently named director of operations for the Center That CARES organization in Pittsburgh. Dallas Black Dance Theatre: Encore! is Home to Point Park Alumni Tuesday, August 25, 2020 \"During my time at Point Park I had the opportunity to work with choreographers from many different backgrounds. The amount of rehearsal and performance experience I acquired in college allowed for a smooth transition into my professional career.\" Alumni Profile Brandon Moon '15 Meet Brandon Moon, a 2015 sports, arts and entertainment management alumnus and owner/creative director for Hippy at Heart Clothing. Alumni Profile Brittany McDonald, Ph.D., '16 '19 Brittany McDonald, an MBA and Ph.D. in community engagement alumna of Point Park University, was named executive director of Uptown Partners of Pittsburgh. Pittsburgh Playhouse Collaboration With City Theatre Produces Plays That Respond to the Current Moment Tuesday, August 4, 2020 Point Park Universityâs Pittsburgh Playhouse and City Theatre Company have launched Homegrown Stories,Â designed to support artists and alumni. Alumni Profile Robelin Bautista '19 Meet Robelin Bautista, a sports, arts and entertainment management December 2019 graduate from El Seibo, Dominican Republic, and Gulf Coast League player development intern for the Toronto Blue Jays Major League Baseball team. Student Profile Lindsey Palmer '15 \"Point Park appealed to me because it offered a city campus, smaller class sizes and a more traditional (darkroom) photography program.\" Alumni Profile Emediong Festus '19 Meet Emediong Festus, a Point Park University 2019 Master of Science in engineering management graduate and project engineer for Intertek in Dallas, Texas. Alumni Profile Kaylee Wong '20 Kaylee Wong '20 was featured as the cover image of a recent Dance Spirit magazine issue. Student Profile Kimberly Crawford-Champion '16 '19 '22 Learn how Kimberly Crawford-Champion, a Point Park Psy.D. in clinical psychology candidate, psychology alumna and veteran is conducting her dissertation research on racial trauma while inspiring African-American youth. Fausto Severino '04 Friday, June 26, 2020 \"My reaction to winning the World Series was to jump around like a mad man and give my wife a big hug and kiss,\" saidÂ Fausto Severino '04, a Point Park University sports, arts and entertainment management alumnus and director of Latin America scouting for the Washington Nationals, who recently received one of the team's World Championship rings. Alumni Profile Rhianna Davis '20 Point Park University business management major Rhianna Davis was hired as an integrated marketing associate for Blender, Inc., right after graduating in April 2020. Alumni Profile Theopolis Washington III '18 Meet Theopolis Washington III, a 2018 instructional studies graduate and paraprofessional for Maple Heights High School in Ohio. Kiki Lucas '99, Assistant Professor of Dance Monday, June 22, 2020 \"I love to ignite passion, dig deep and demand performance quality. I am good at reading the energy of my classroom and being able to give the style that I feel best suits that day.\" Alumni Profile Frederick Livingston '15 '18 Meet Frederick Livingston, police officer for Edgewood Borough, and a graduate of Point Park University's B.S. in criminal justice and M.S. in criminal justice administration programs. Alumnus Matt Adams is an Associate Photo Editor for National Geographic Monday, June 1, 2020 \"If I didn't go to Point Park, then I can honestly say that I wouldn't be in the job I am in now. It was the starting point to an incredible journey.\" Alumni Profile Dominique Hildebrand '16 \"As an associate photo editor, it is my responsibility to source images for daily production, breaking news and short feature picture stories. Often, I spend my time trying to illustrate a story that has not been photographed or even more often, cannot be photographed.\" Alumni Profile Jeff Eakins '19 Meet Jeff Eakins, a graduate of Point Park University's ABCTE program and seventh grade ELA teacher for Bermudian Springs School District. Alumni Profile Samiar Nefzi '19 Meet School of Communication alumnus Samiar Nefzi '19, a reporter/fill-in anchor at WJET/WFXP in Erie, Pa. Alumni Profile Anthony DiCarolis '18 Meet MBA alumnus Anthony DiCarolis, financial analyst II for the computer software company Synopsys. Point Park University's Honors Program Celebrates Class of 2020 Friday, April 24, 2020 \"The Honors Program has motivated me to be a better student and person. While challenging myself academically in classes, I was also encouraged to volunteer and engage with the Pittsburgh community. As a senior looking back, I know the Honors Program has made me a better student and a better member of my community,\" said Alexa Newbrough, a senior theatre arts major. Alumni Profile Shawn Lesniak '18 \"Because of my training at Point Park, I was able to watch, learn and perform various styles of dance. The faculty did an amazing job at creating a space for aspiring artists like myself to hone their skills and explore, in depth, what it even means to be an artist.\" Honors Program: Together Apart, Only a Virtual Meeting Away Wednesday, April 15, 2020 âWe wanted to make sure that we congratulated our seniors as we always do at our final meeting of the semester. It is very important to me as the adviser because they work so hard inside and outside their classrooms. We have managed to maintain contact in many ways with our honors students as they finish out this unusual semester. This just seemed to be natural,â said Helen Fallon, director of Point Park's Honors Program. Alumni Profile Blaine King '17 '20 \"I was attracted to the hands-on experience I would get from the start as a broadcast major. For my MBA, the online experience allowed me to work at a pace that was logical for my school, work and personal life.\" Lisa Pickett, Ed.D.,'18 Monday, April 13, 2020 Point Park University Ed.D. in leadership and administration alumna Lisa Pickett '18,Â English department director forÂ The Pittsburgh School for the Creative and Performing Arts,Â was published in the April 2020 issue of the academicÂ peer-reviewed journal, The Urban Review, for her article,Â \"Three Trains Running: The Intersectionality of RaceâBased Trauma, African American Youth, and RaceâBased Interventions.\" Alumni Profile Diane Nutbrown '20 Meet Diane Nutbrown, Ph.D., a graduate of Point Park University's ABCTE program and a chemistry and physics teacher for The Neighborhood Academy. Alumni Profile Casey Hoolahan '18 \"My experience with student media like U-View and The Globe were vital in preparing me to be the one-man band that is a multimedia journalist. Those groups pushed me to refine my writing and video skills and to find my own stories to tell â independence is vital as a reporter in a small town,\" said Casey Hoolahan '18. Alumni Profile Lee Schmidt '16 Meet Lee Schmidt, a public administration alumnus who was recently promoted to assistant director of operations for the Pittsburgh Public Safety department. Pittsburgh Playhouse Launches Online Portals for Sharing Art and Performance Monday, April 6, 2020 #PghPlayhouseArtShare is an online portal providing a showcase for performing artists, including Point Park students, alumni and professionals to share an artistic creation. Submissions can include a poem, movie, song, personal monologue, photography or dance combination. Chosen selections will be shared on the Pittsburgh Playhouse and Point Park University social media channels. Alumni Profile Cassandra Scannella '16 Meet Cassandra Scannella, an instructional designer for Columbia University in NYC, who earned a Master of Arts degree in curriculum and instruction, with a focus in adult learning and training, fully online from Point Park. Alumni Profile Jeremey Toth '16 Rowland School of Business alumnus and business relationship banker Jeremey Toth was named a Citizen of Excellence Award winner by Citizens Bank. Women Veterans Event Hosted by History and Honors Programs Features World War II Codebreaker Monday, March 16, 2020 Veterans were honored at Point Park University for Womenâs History Month with an event hosted by the history and Honors programs featuring 99-year-old Julia Parsons, a codebreaker from World War II. 2020 NHSDF Highlights Tuesday, March 3, 2020 National High School Dance Festival at Point Park University included three exhilarating days of classes, auditions, performances and making new friends from around the world. Alumni Profile Miles Ritenour '10 \"Never stop learning. Soak up as much as you can in the classroom, but actually get out and do the job you want to do. You can only learn so much in the classroom, so intern, shadow people you admire, ask for advice from professors and people who have done what you want to do.\" Point Park Universityâs Pittsburgh Playhouse Presents The Wolves Friday, February 21, 2020 The Pittsburgh Playhouse welcomes home alumna Rachel M. Stevens, a New York City-based director, teaching artist and acting coach, to direct The Wolves. Alumni Profile Scott Garing '17 Meet Scott Garing, online public administration graduate and the new chief of fire and emergency services for Cranberry Township, Pa. Making Music Industry Connections: SAEM Students Selected to Attend Pollstar Live! 2020 Conference in Beverly Hills Friday, February 14, 2020 Ten Point Park University sports, arts and entertainment management students were selected to attend Pollstar LIVE! 2020Â â the music industryâs largest conference in the United States â held Feb. 4-6 in Beverly Hills, Calif. Julie Bowser '19 Thursday, February 13, 2020 From applicants across the nation, the Country Music Association selected Point Park University alumna Julie Bowser '19, as its United States inaugural participant of the Rob Potts International Exchange Program for individuals pursuing a career in the country music industry.Â Alumni Profile Nuhu Okikiri '19 Meet Nuhu Okikiri, a 2019 international MBA alumnus and data analyst for FedEx Ground in Pittsburgh. Alumni Profile Alexander Popichak '18 \"My professors helped me polish my resume, reel and website before applying to various newsrooms. Before going to Point Park, I had no idea what a producer was or did, but after talking with professors over the years, it was clear that I loved this kind of work and was connected to Erie News Now by one of my professors.\" - Alexander Popichak '18 Alumni Profile Annie Morgan '18 \"The faculty recognized my potential and pushed me beyond what I thought I was capable of. I felt nurtured and cared for â both as an artist and a human being.\" Alumni Profile Joshua Mitchell '17 Meet Point Park University MBA graduate Joshua Mitchell, a veteran and CEO/founder of Improvyze, LLC. Alumni Profile Braxton Bragg '19 Meet Braxton Bragg, a 2019 M.S. in health care administration and management alumnus, who was recently promoted to intermediate improvement specialist for UPMC. Alumni Profile Christie Lewis, Ed.D., '18 Meet Christie Lewis, Ed.D., Point Park University Ed.D. alumna, education programs and field placement specialist, Act 48 coordinator and adjunct professor, who received the Outstanding Dissertation of the Year award from The Pennsylvania Association of Colleges and Teacher Educators Conference. Alumni Profile Michael Harding '14 '20 Meet Michael Harding, MBA alumnus and Ph.D. in community engagement student who was recently promoted to director of business engagement at Carnegie Mellon University. Alumni Profile Emily Bezbatchenko '18 \"Point Park prepared me in the best way possible for company work post-graduation. The training in all styles made the switch between ballet, modern and jazz effortless.\" Alumni Profile Madeline King '19 Meet Madeline King, a spring 2019 graduate and staff auditor for the CPA accounting firm Maher Duessel in Pittsburgh. Alumni Profile Wade Tucker '15 Meet Point Park University information technology alumnus Wade Tucker, founder of the web/mobile application company TrendTeams. Major League Baseball Players Don Kelly â06 and Neil Walker Chat With SAEM Sports Agents Class Monday, November 25, 2019 Major League Baseball players alumnus Don Kelly '06, now a first base coach for the Houston Astros, and Neil Walker, an infielder for the Miami Marlins, led a conversation with Sports, Arts and Entertainment Management Instructor Chuck Berryâs Sports Agents class. Point Park Welcomes Former U.S. Ambassador and Award-Winning Middle East Travel Specialist Monday, November 18, 2019 Former U.S. Ambassador to Yemen, senior vice president of the Middle East Institute and Point Park alumnus Gerald Feierstein â73, and Islamic culture writer, blogger and award-winning travel specialist Carolyn McIntyre, recently gave engaging presentations at Point Park University on U.S. policy in the Middle East and Yemeni architecture, respectively. Conservatory Theatre Company Presents Much Ado About Nothing Friday, November 15, 2019 Point Park Universityâs Conservatory Theatre Company features Shakespeareâs classic with a twist, Much Ado About Nothing, Nov. 8-17 in the PNC Theatre at the Pittsburgh Playhouse. Alumni Profile James Ogden II '12 Theatre production (stage-management) alumnus James Ogden's resume includes SeaWorld San Antonio, Charlotte Ballet, Martha Graham Dance Company, Elisa Monte Dance, Complexions Contemporary Ballet and Alonzo King LINES Ballet. Alumni Profile James Nusser '17 '19 Meet adult learner James Nusser, a 2017 accounting and 2019 MBA alumnus, and now a senior tax analyst for Vitro Architectural Glass. Alumni Profile Alumna and Former Rockette Eileen Grace Hosts Workshop at Point Park \"As dancers we need to always strive to be better and to continue training with a keen eye. DedicationÂ andÂ commitmentÂ are key as well as letting your passion shine throughÂ with confidence.\" Alumni Profile Carley Bonk '19 \"Make the most of the opportunities provided in college to get your work published. It is so essential to have a hefty portfolio when applying for that first real job.\" Alumni Profile Tyler Matylewicz '16 \"Your career is purely dependent on your attitude, outlook on life and experiences learned; so soak up as much as you can at Point Park. The program offers you an extremely wide variety of opportunities that prepare you for anything.\" Alumni Profile Raymond Houston, Ed.D., '04 Alumnus Raymond Houston, Ed.D., who earned a Master of Arts in curriculum and instruction focused in adult learning and training from Point Park, was named dean of the School of Mathematics, Science and Engineering at SUNY Westchester Community College. Alumni Profile Ryan Yorgen '17 \"Point Park has been instrumental in leading me to land my dream job. Everyone who is a part of the School of Communication was committed to helping me reach my goals.\" Calculating Career Success: Tax Principals Featured at Women In Industry Speaker Series Event Friday, September 27, 2019 The Rowland School of Business welcomed to campus tax principals Celeste Suchko, CPA, and Mandy Merchant, CPA, from CliftonLarsonAllen â the eighth largest accountancy firm in the United States â as part of its Women In Industry Speaker Series. Alumni Profile Beatrice Contreras '19 Meet Beatrice Contreras, a 2019 MBA alumna and international relationship manager for PNC. Alumni Profile Andrew Wright '12 \"I thrived on the diversity of classes and made sure to continue my training in jazz, modern and ballet throughout my entire time at Point Park. This diversity really helped me to develop a versatility that benefits me to this day,\" said Andrew Wright, 2012 B.F.A. in dance alumnus. The Point Summer 2019 Friday, September 6, 2019 Highlights include: Point Park and pro sports teams kick off premier esports event, Pittsburgh Playhouse 2019-20 season, education students teach in Ireland and much more. Alumni Profile Sierra Tufts '15 Sierra Tufts, a 2015 School of Communication alumna, is an anchor/reporter for WANE 15 in Indiana. Alumni Profile Robert Maley '19 Meet Robert Maley, a 2019 MBA alumnus and vice president and specialist of SAR Investigations for BNY Mellon in Downtown Pittsburgh. Alumni Profile Emily Kelly '19 Meet Emily Kelly, a sports, arts and entertainment management alumna working in the box offices for the Pittsburgh Cultural Trust and the Pittsburgh Symphony Orchestra. Alumni Profile Jessica Martin '17 '19 Meet Jessica Martin, a 2017 SAEM and 2019 MBA alumna who was promoted full time to an inside sales representative by the Pittsburgh Penguins. Alumni Profile Alex Britton Peterson '13 Meet 2013 broadcast reporting alumnus Alex Britton Peterson, a reporter and anchor for ABC27 News in Harrisburg. Alumni Profile Adebomi Enitan '18 Meet Adebomi Enitan, a 2018 Master of Science in engineering management graduate and an electrical engineer for Pioneer Power Group in Warrendale, Pa. Alumni Profile Megan Mussomeli '09 SAEM alumna Megan Mussomeli was promoted to lead strategic projects for the entertainment management software company, Cvent. Alumni Profile Rebekah Mohrmann '18 Meet Rebekah Mohrmann, a 2018 sports, arts and entertainment management alumna and media, graphics and promotions assistant for the Salem Red Sox in Salem, Va. From Steel City to Music City: Point Park Pioneers Launching Careers in Nashville Wednesday, July 17, 2019 More than half a dozen Point Park graduates have moved to Nashville to begin their careers in entertainment management. Alumni Profile Hannah James '16 Meet film production alumna Hannah James, a video coordinator for Little League International. Alumni Profile Calyx Deroche '19 Calyx Deroche earned a B.A. in cinema production in three years at Point Park. Before graduating, she interned at WQED and was recently hired as a Next Generation Fellow, an intensive training program for aspiring content creators. Alumni Profile Marissa Cerully '18 Point Park University K-12 principal certification graduate Marissa Cerully was recently appointed assistant principal by the Spring Cove School District. Alumni Profile Brittany Hoke '10 \"I think Point Park is one of the most well-connected schools in the area. Our professors worked in the industry inÂ Pittsburgh, which is huge. Learning from them and being able to go to them for advice long after graduation day has been invaluable.\" - Brittany Hoke, anchor/reporter, WTAE-TV Alumni Profile Anthony Romano '19 Anthony Romano earned a Bachelor of Science degree in electrical engineering this past spring and was promoted to application engineer at Benshaw, Inc. Alumni Profile Andrew Duncan '18 '19 Meet Andrew Duncan, a 2018 business management alumna and MBA student, who was hired by Point Park alumna Shannon Gregg '14 as a partner account manager for Cloud Adoption Solutions. Alumni Profile Gabe Reed '18 Gabe Reed, 2018 Pioneer Records artist winner and musical theatre graduate, recently placed second in the International Songwriting Competition's unpublished category. Alumni Profile Miranda Van Bramer '17 Meet School of Communication alumna Miranda Van Bramer, on-air talent and promotions assistant for BIG 104.7 FM/iHeartMedia Pittsburgh. International Media Class Visits United Kingdom Thursday, June 13, 2019 Point Park University students in the International Media class traveled to London, Windsor, Stratford, Liverpool, Manchester and Edinburgh May 5-17, 2019. Alumni Profile Andrea Robinson '09 Meet Andrea Robinson, Point Park University MBA graduate and owner of Sugar and Smoke restaurant. Alumni Profile Stephanie White '18 Meet Ed.D. alumna Stephanie White, a national board-certified English teacher for West Allegheny School District. Alumni Profile Nina Belcastro '16 Meet Nina Belcastro, a 2016 online organizational leadership graduate of Point Park University and manager of the Township of Baldwin in Pittsburgh. Alumni Profile Will McMinn '12 Meet MBA alumnus Will McMinn, a business development executive for RxBenefits, Inc. Alumni Profile Lily Pruneda '18 Meet Lily Pruneda, a 2018 Point Park elementary education alumna and first grade teacher for Broward County Public Schools in Florida. Alumni Profile Jenea Brooks '15 Meet Jenea Brooks, a 2015 Point Park University instructional studies transfer alumna and owner/director of Creative Community, LLC, Early Learning Center. Alumni Profile William Utzman '00 Meet William Utzman, PE, CPESC, a transfer civil engineering technology alumnus and president of Morris Knowles & Associates, Inc. Student Profile Laura Ward '19 Meet Laura Ward, Ed.D. in leadership and administration doctoral student and high school librarian for Fox Chapel Area School District. Pittsburgh Playhouse Announces Bold, Innovative 2019-20 Season Tuesday, April 30, 2019 âOur first season laid the groundwork for creating innovative theatrical opportunities that offered students the opportunity to experience what itâs like to mount a new work alongside a professional artistic team, while at the same time, bringing exceptional and entertaining productions to Pittsburgh audiences,â said Paul Hennigan, Ed.D., president of Point Park. Alumni Michael Spagnoletti and Judge Guido DeAngelis Honored by Criminal Justice Club Monday, April 22, 2019 The Criminal Justice Club at Point Park University hosted a celebration dinner in honor of alumniÂ Michael Spagnoletti, â18, and Judge Guido DeAngelis, J.D., â80. School of Communication Graduates Part of Pulitzer Prize-Winning Team Wednesday, April 17, 2019 School of Communication graduates Ashley Murray, M.A., and Andrew Goldstein are part of the Pittsburgh Post-GazetteÂ team honored with a 2019 Pulitzer Prize for breaking news reporting. Alumni Profile Kidde Kokole '18 Meet Kidde Kokole, a 2018 Point Park University English graduate and Native Guest English Teacher for the English Program in Korea (EPIK). Alumni Profile Nick Davignon '18 After earning a master's degree in secondary education from Point Park University, Nick Davignon was hired by South Fayette High School as a long-term biology substitute teacher. Top 10 CNN Hero Honoree, City Housing Authority Official Speaking at 2019 Graduation Thursday, April 11, 2019 Point Park University will celebrate the annual Hooding and Degree Conferral and Commencement ceremonies Saturday, April 27 at PPG Paints Arena. Alumni Profile Ryan Bailey '14 \"I'm lucky enough to have been part of the first wave of esports talent. I'm one of the few who has a degree in broadcasting and real experience in a TV studio. I hope that more Point Park students can make their mark across the industry.\" Literary Arts and Social Justice Studies Department Presents Panel on Careers in Writing Thursday, April 4, 2019 The Department of Literary Arts and Social Justice at Point Park University hosted a career panel session March 28 featuring creative writing alumna Paige Mastrippolito â17, as well as writing professionals Maureen Passmore and Mariana Padias.Â History and Honors Programs Host Korean War Veterans Storytelling Session Monday, March 25, 2019 More than 150 Point Park University students, veterans, and members and guests of PittsburghâsÂ Veterans Breakfast Club attended a KoreanÂ War Veterans Storytelling Session March 20 on campus. Regional Premiere at Prime Stage Theatre Features Point Park University Alumni and Students Wednesday, February 27, 2019 \"Itâs comforting and exciting to see Point Park fostering connections with professional theaters. Itâs an example of the fact that training is working; script analysis, movement, and voice and speech are all pivotal to telling this story with justice,\" said Vanessa Vivas, theatre major. Alumni Profile Emily Marburger '10 '12 Meet Emily Marburger, mayor of Bellevue and a journalism and mass communication, history and MBA alumna of Point Park University. Alumni Profile Suzie Cool, M.A., '18 Meet Suzie Cool, M.A. in media communication alumna. Cool is manager of marketing and promotions, on-field host and color commentator for the Salem Red Sox. Alumni Profile Chelsey Driskel '17 '18 Meet Chelsey Driskel, B.A. in public relations and advertising and M.A. in intelligence and global security alumna, who was hired as a government contracts specialist by WESCO International, Inc. Alumni Profile Gabriel Florentino '18 2018 musical theatre alumnus Gabriel Florentino plays 'Manolin' in the world premiere stage adaptation of \"The Old Man and the Sea\" at the Pittsburgh Playhouse. Alumni Profile Miranda Peel '18 Meet Miranda Peel, a 2018 sports, arts and entertainment management alumna and guest experience services professional intern for Walt Disney World Parks and Resorts. Alumni Profile Annie Fiffick '16 Meet Annie Fiffick, 2016 Master of Science in criminal justice administration and food pantry director for Community Human Services. Student Profile Lauren Shoenberger '14 '19 Lauren Shoenberger, a 2014 business management alumna and M.S. in health care administration and management