e helped Jocelyn Hyrb '17, land her current position as a radio promotions manager. Alumni Profile Erica Messonnier \"Point Park shaped me into the performer I am today. The school provided me with all the tools I needed to become a professional performer. I am forever grateful for everyone who helped me achieve my dreams.\" Alumni Profile Fausto Severino '04 Meet Fausto Severino, Latin America Crosschecker for the Washington Nationals and SAEM 2004 graduate. Alumni Profile Alumni Profile: David Flora, Senior Producer/Editor, Detroit Pistons \"I believe I landed my current job because of my education and experiences in the field. I also made sure to have a clean and concise resume as well as a solid demo reel.\" Alumni Profile M.B.A. Alumna is Director of Communications for Central Catholic Learn how an M.B.A. degree from Point Park helped Chelsey Rovesti land her current position. Alumni Profile Shannon Shields, M.A. \"Changing careers was one of the best decisions Iâve ever made. Getting my masterâs degree from Point Park was the catalyst that allowed me to make that change,\" said Shannon Shields. Public Administration Program Celebrates its Alumni With Reunion on Campus Monday, December 18, 2017 From fire chiefs and EMS professionals to business and borough administrators, alumni from a variety of service professions were warmly welcomed at Point Park University's public administration reunion event. International M.B.A. Alumna Leading Information Technology Projects for PNC Wednesday, December 6, 2017 Meet Trupti Tamore, release testing manager for Kforce Consulting with PNC Financial Services. Alumni Profile Annie A. Pugh '17 Meet Annie A. Pugh, a fourth grade teacher at Lincoln Elementary, part of the Mt. Lebanon School District. Art Management Careers: Point Park Graduates Working for The Andy Warhol Museum Thursday, November 30, 2017 In their roles at The Andy Warhol Museum, alumnae Charlene Bidula and Lena Tavoletti are directly applying the knowledge 