      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at Point Park | Point Park University | Pittsburgh, PA Skip to main content Menu Menu In this section In this section Apply Request Info About Us Academics Admissions & Financial Aid Career-ready Student Life Give Now Search Search Apply Request Info Events Calendar A-Z Quicklinks My Point Park Contact Us Careers at Point Park Income and Employment Verification Dining On Campus Careers at Point Park Dynamic workplace, rewarding opportunities Point Park University welcomes your interest in our employment opportunities and strives to attract top candidates for our job openings. Point Park University is a private, urban university with nearly 4,000 undergraduate and graduate students at our campus in Downtown Pittsburgh. The University employs more than 400 full-time and 400 part-time faculty and staff, who enjoy a unique culture of higher education while working together to support our University's mission, vision and values . Employment Listings Point Park University welcomes your interest in employment opportunities and encourages you to review open positions. Please note that Point Park University does not accept unsolicited applications. Student Employment Graduate assistantships Student employment Benefits Point Park University offers a competitive benefits package for full-time employees. Part-time employees are eligible for limited benefits. Full-time Faculty Part-time Faculty Full-time Staff Part-time Staff Secretarial/Clerical Union Employees International Union of Operating Engineers Employees University Policies Point Park University adheres to a non-discrimination policy, recognizes its responsibility to create and maintain an environment that affirms diversity, and has an employee Code of Conduct. For details on each of these areas, follow the links below: Non-discrimination Policy Code of Conduct Diversity Statement State and Federal Wage and Labor Law Employment and Income Verifications We have partnered with The Work Number® from Equifax, which is a simple, quick, and more private way to help get your employment and income information to companies wh en neede d. C lick here for more details! Annual Security Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act, the Point Park University Public Safety Department provides information on crime statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues on the Point Park University campus. For more information, view the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . For a paper copy of the report, contact the Point Park University Public Safety Department at 412-392-3960. Point Park University 201 Wood Street Pittsburgh, PA 15222-1984 Careers at Point Park Location & Directions Non-discrimination Policy Privacy Policy Ready to learn more? Request information Plan a visit Take a virtual tour Calculate financial aid Follow Us tiktok instagram facebook Linkedin Â youtube Â Apply Now"
    }
